/* Super SAT — Vocabook, Reading Time, Fight Time. Original content, extracted verbatim from Super SAT.html. */
const VB={"cp":[[["Unpredictable, inconsistent, irregular","His erratic dance moves were so unpredictable that even the DJ couldn’t keep up with the beat","Predictable"],["Hard to reach, hidden away","The WiFi signal was so bad in the secluded cabin that they had to make friends with the squirrels just for entertainment","Accessible"],["To rise and fall irregularly","His mood fluctuates like the stock market — happy when he gets pizza, but plummeting when it runs out.","Stabilize"],["To praise, to worship","She exalted her coffee maker every morning, whispering, “You are my hero,” as it brewed her life-saving caffeine","Criticize"],["To warn or scold someone","The cat was admonished for knocking over the vase, but its smug face said, “I regret nothing!”","Praise"],["Sudden, unexpected, without warning","His abrupt decision to cut his hair at 3 a.m. left him looking like a porcupine in a windstorm.","Gradual"],["Satisfied","After eating an entire pizza by himself, he was so content that even the thought of dessert couldn’t move him.","Discontent"],["Uncommon, strange","His eccentric habit of wearing socks over his shoes made people think he was either a genius or just really confused","Conventional"],["Stuck in mud","She was so mired in paperwork that even a bulldozer wouldn’t be able to dig her out of her office.","Free"],["Used in casual conversation","His speech was so full of colloquial slang that even his grandma said, “Bruh, I don’t understand you.”","Formal"],["Settle one’s differences, make compatible, bring back to peace","They finally reconciled after their epic debate over whether pineapple belongs on pizza. Spoiler: It doesn’t","Estrange"],["To cause someone to feel isolated or lonely","His decision to start every conversation with a detailed history of traffic lights quickly alienated all his friends","Befriend"],["To tell the difference between","He could barely distinguish between his identical twin brothers until one started wearing neon green socks every day.","Confuse"],["Sufficient, enough, acceptable","His cooking skills were adequate—let’s just say the fire alarm got a workout, but the pizza wasn’t that burnt.","Inadequate"],["1) To deal with someone or something 2) To claim or state a belief confidently","He contended with his alarm clock every morning as if it was a fierce battle between sleep and reality.","Surrender"],["Having doubts","She was skeptical about the “miracle” face cream that claimed to make her look 20 years younger overnight.","Trusting"],["To give the right to vote","The town held a parade to celebrate when they finally enfranchised the local raccoons… though they immediately voted for more trash cans.","Disenfranchise, enslave"],["1) Having a lot of worldly experience and knowledge 2) Complicated","His sophisticated taste in cheese made him the only person who actually knew what “gorgonzola” was at the party.","naive"],["1) Thorough, complete, extensive 2) Fundamental, essential 3) Revolutionary, extreme","His radical idea to solve all the world’s problems by making every Friday “Free Ice Cream Day” was met with mixed","Conservative"],["To create or think up","She formulated a foolproof plan to sneak past her dog—step one: tiptoe; step two: realize dogs can hear everything","Destroy"],["To confirm or verify","He could attest to the fact that eating 10 tacos in one sitting was not a good life decision.","Deny"],["Annoying, irritating","The constant buzzing of the fly around his head was so vexing that he considered giving it a name just to yell at it properly.","Pleasing"],["Humble, low-key","The unassuming librarian turned out to be a ninja in her free time, proving you can’t judge a book by its cover","Arrogant"],["To pressure or force someone to do something","He coerced his little brother into trading his chocolate bar for a carrot by promising it was “just as tasty.” It wasn’t.","Persuade (gently)"],["Very skilled at something","She was so adept at parallel parking that she could fit a bus into a space meant for a bicycle.","Inept, mediocre, amateur"]],[["Fluent or persuasive in speaking or writing","His speech was so eloquent that even his dog stopped barking just to listen","Inarticulate, dullness"],["Plain and without decoration, comforts, or anything extra","Her living room was so austere that the only decoration was a single chair—perfect for minimalist extreme sports.","Ornate, Luxurious"],["To fear, be afraid of","He dreaded his mom’s reaction to the broken vase, but he blamed the wind—inside the house.","Welcome, Anticipate"],["Unavoidable","It was inevitable that he would trip while texting and walking, as everyone saw it coming—except him","Avoidable, Uncertain"],["To emphasize","She stressed the importance of cleaning the room, but it still looked like a tornado had moved in.","Downplay, Minimize"],["To produce, generate, or create","The idea for his movie spawned after a dream where penguins took over the world with dance battles","Destroy, Terminate"],["To give up, deny, or surrender something","He renounced his superhero cape after one too many failed attempts at flying off the couch.","Accept, Embrace"],["Never done or known before","His unprecedented move to start a cheese museum in his basement had the neighbors curiously excited.","Common, Routine"],["To bring up a difficult subject for discussion","He broached the subject of missing rent with his landlord, who thankfully had a sense of humor—about everything except rent.","Avoid, Suppress"],["A person authorized to act on","He sent his dog as a proxy to the","Principal, Original"],["Harmful, damaging","Eating 10 donuts for breakfast might be detrimental to your health, but it’s great for your mood—temporarily.","Beneficial, Constructive"],["Having no religious or spiritual basis","The concert was entirely secular, except for the part where the lead singer thanked “the universe” for his fans","Sacred, Religious"],["New and different","His innovative way of organizing his closet involved attaching his shirts to a ceiling fan—one quick spin, and he was dressed","Unoriginal, Traditional"],["Real and able to be shown or touched","The excitement in the room was so tangible, you could practically high-five it.","Intangible, Abstract"],["To spread widely (particularly information)","He tried to disseminate the news about the school trip, but it somehow turned into a rumor about a school-wide pizza party","Conceal, Contain"],["To assign a task to another person","He delegated the dishwashing duty to his little brother, but somehow the dishes were still dirty, and the brother was missing","Retain, Withhold"],["Clearly visible or understood; obvious","It became apparent that he had no idea how to assemble the furniture when the bookshelf started resembling a chair","Hidden, Obscure"],["To suggest or propose something","He postulated that pizza should be considered a vegetable, which earned him both laughs and several high-fives","Reject, Deny"],["To guess, to form a theory without firm evidence","He speculated that his lost sock had fallen into a black hole because where else could it have gone?","Prove, Verify"],["A market selling a large variety of goods","The bazaar had everything from handmade rugs to pet unicorn horns—for cats, of course.","Boutique, Supermarket"],["Scattered, irregular, unpredictable","His sporadic attempts to clean his room usually started strong and ended with him watching TV in the mess","Consistent, Regular"],["The right to vote","She celebrated when women gained suffrage by voting for the cutest puppy in the election for “Pet of the Year.”","Disenfranchisement, Disqualification"],["Unwilling or unable to believe something","He was incredulous when his cat finally learned how to fetch. “Next up,” he said, “playing the piano.”","Believing, Gullible"],["Unrealistically aiming for perfection","His idealistic goal of becoming a world-class chef in a week ended when he burned toast—three times in a row","Realistic, Pragmatic"],["To mix or combine into one (typically ideas)","He conflated his birthday party with Halloween, so everyone showed up in costumes to celebrate his “vampire cake.”","Separate, Divide"]],[["Poverty, scarcity","The paucity of snacks at the party led to a fierce competition over the last slice of pizza","Abundance, Plentifulness"],["Temporary, short-lived","His enthusiasm for working out was ephemeral—lasting just long enough to post about it on social media","Permanent, Lasting"],["To cause (someone) to take a course of action","The sight of chocolate cake promptly caused him to break his diet with zero hesitation","Discourage, Deter"],["Deep respect for someone or something","He showed great reverence for his grandma’s cooking, bowing before every plate of lasagna like it was a royal feast","Disrespect, Scorn"],["A great difference","The disparity between his baking skills and his sister’s was obvious when his cookies looked like rocks and hers like art","Similarity, Equality"],["Not influenced by strong emotion, fair-minded","As the judge, she remained dispassionate, even when the defendant made a very emotional argument about losing his last donut","Emotional, Biased"],["A noteworthy occurrence or situation","The sudden appearance of a double rainbow after the storm was such a phenomenon that everyone stopped to take selfies with it","Ordinary, Normality"],["To brag, to show off","He boasted so much about his new car that his friends started pretending they couldn’t hear him","Humble, Conceal"],["Irritating, annoying","The irksome sound of his neighbor’s endless lawn mowing made him wish grass would just stop growing","Pleasant, Agreeable"],["To suggest or call attention to indirectly, to make a reference to something","She alluded to the surprise party by “accidentally” mentioning how much she loved cake in every conversation","State Directly, Declare"],["Having unlimited or great power","He felt a sense of omnipotence when he finally found the TV remote, as if he could control the whole universe","Powerlessness, Weakness"],["To cause a reaction or emotion (usually anger); to trigger","His joke about pineapple on pizza provoked a heated debate that threatened to divide the whole group of friends","Pacify, Calm"],["To allow oneself to enjoy the pleasure of","He decided to indulge in a whole tub of ice cream after a long day of pretending to eat salads.","Abstain, Deny"],["Firmly established and unlikely to change","His entrenched belief that socks and sandals were the height of fashion would not be swayed by any amount of ridicule","Flexible, Unstable"],["Built-in, existing in something as a permanent or essential characteristic","His inherent love of naps made him the best couch tester in the world","Acquired, External"],["Everyday informal language, local dialect","He quickly picked up the local vernacular, casually saying “y’all” after just one day in Texas.","Formal Language, Literary Language"],["Interrogation, questioning","His mom’s inquisition about his missing homework felt more intense than a detective show","Neglect, Ignorance"],["A short personal story","He told an amusing anecdote about the time he accidentally walked into the wrong Zoom meeting—and stayed for an hour","Epic, Long Narrative"],["Evil in nature, harmful","The villain’s malign plot to steal all the world’s ice cream was met with global outrage","Benevolent, Kind"],["Oddity, something that is not normal","His punctuality was such an anomaly that everyone asked if he was feeling okay when he arrived on time","Normality, Usualness"],["To hold someone or something back, to suppress, to prevent","His fear of public speaking inhibited him from raising his","Encourage, Allow"],["Changeable","His mutable schedule meant that nobody ever knew when he’d actually show up","Fixed, Stable"],["1) Of little importance 2) Caring too much about trivial matters","The argument over whose turn it was to pick a movie was so petty that even the dog rolled his eyes","Significant, Important"],["Passionate about something","He was such an avid collector of rare comic books that he could smell a first edition from a mile away.","Indifferent, Apathetic"],["To call on or refer to something","He tried to invoke the “5-second rule” after dropping his sandwich, but it was too late—the dog already had it","Dismiss, Ignore"]],[["Foolish, reckless","His imprudent decision to race a shopping cart down the hill ended exactly as you’d expect: with him in a bush.","Wise, Cautious"],["Persistence, determination","His tenacity in building a treehouse was admirable, especially since he only had one hammer and an entire tree full of squirrels to deal with","Weakness, Indifference"],["Respected","The venerable professor was so respected that even the campus squirrels lined up to listen to his lectures","Disrespected, Dishonorable"],["Enforcing strict obedience to authority","The authoritarian teacher had such strict rules that even whispering in class felt like a major rebellion","Democratic, Permissive"],["An angry argument or disagreement","Their quarrel over the last slice of cake was so intense that it ended with forks in the air like swords","Agreement, Harmony"],["1) To produce or generate (a result) 2) To surrender","His hard work yielded excellent results, but he still had to yield to his little brother in their pillow fight","Resist, Defy"],["Having mixed feelings","She felt ambivalent about the movie, loving the action scenes but hating the long romantic subplot","Decisive, Certain"],["To try hard to do something","He endeavored to bake a perfect cake, but somehow it turned into a pancake instead","Give up, Neglect"],["A violent uprising or rebellion","The squirrels staged an insurrection in the park, stealing every picnic basket in sight","Peace, Submission"],["To think about for a long time","He spent hours contemplating the meaning of life—or at least","Ignore, Dismiss"],["To force someone to do something","His love for dessert compelled him to eat three slices of cake, even though he was already full","Discourage, Dissuade"],["Possible to do easily or conveniently","It wasn’t exactly feasible to finish all his homework in one night, but a lot of snacks helped","Impossible, Unworkable"],["An opinion or conclusion that is unproven, a guess","His conjecture that aliens stole his homework was a little far-fetched, but who’s to say for sure","Fact, Proof"],["Based on random choice or personal impulse, rather than any reason or system","His decision to wear a suit to the beach was completely arbitrary and confused everyone, including the lifeguard","Reasoned, Logical"],["To make stronger","He reinforced the pillow fort with extra blankets, ensuring it could survive even the fiercest of sibling attacks","Weaken, Undermine"],["To serve as a neutralizing or counterbalancing force to something","She tempered the spicy chili with a spoonful of sour cream, saving everyone’s taste buds from certain doom","Intensify, Aggravate"],["An official order or command","The king issued a decree that all homework be completed before dessert, much to the children’s dismay","Suggestion, Request"],["Concise use of words in writing or speech","His brevity in giving directions was impressive, but it left everyone more confused than ever","Verbosity, Lengthiness"],["Open to more than one interpretation; unclear","His equivocal answer about whether he ate the last cookie made it clear he was definitely guilty","Clear, Definite"],["A place that is strongly defended, a fortress","The treehouse became their stronghold during the epic neighborhood water balloon fight","Weakness, Vulnerability"],["To form or create a plan or idea","He conceived a brilliant plan to","Destroy, Neglect"],["Excessive pride in one’s own appearance or achievements","His vanity was so intense that he carried a mirror in his pocket just to check his reflection every five minutes","Humility, Modesty"],["Slow-moving","He was so sluggish after Thanksgiving dinner that even his attempt to get off the couch felt like an Olympic event","Energetic, Quick"],["Instinct, the ability to understand something immediately","Her intuition told her that the pie would be delicious, even though it looked slightly questionable","Logic, Reason"],["Impossible to stop or prevent","The inexorable march of time eventually led him to the sad realization that all the ice cream was gone","Flexible, Stoppable"]],[["To cause or give rise to (a feeling, situation, or condition)","His unexpected compliment engendered a wave of confidence that carried her through the entire day","Suppress, Prevent"],["A person’s nature, character, or frame of mind","His easygoing temperament made him the perfect mediator during family game night—especially when Monopoly got intense","Irritability, Volatility"],["A sudden change or disruption, chaos","The surprise snowstorm caused such an upheaval that even the snowmen were caught off guard","Stability, Calm"],["To welcome with open arms, to accept or support willingly","He embraced the idea of a pajama day at work, showing up in a full onesie without hesitation","Reject, Shun"],["To show to be true","He tried to substantiate his claim that aliens ate his homework by showing a blurry UFO picture—but no one was convinced.","Disprove, Refute"],["Shallow, on the surface","His knowledge of French was superficial, limited to knowing how to order croissants and say “bonjour.”","Deep, Thorough"],["Supreme power or authority","The sovereignty of the tiny nation was symbolized by its proud flag, which was carried everywhere—even to picnics","Subordination, Powerlessness"],["Luxurious","The birthday party was so lavish, it had a chocolate fountain, fireworks, and a live band—just for the dog","Frugal, Modest"],["The essence, the main point","The crux of the mystery was solved when they realized the butler had been stealing all the cookies","Detail, Side issue"],["Lack of interest and concern","His indifference toward the new movie was clear—he spent more time looking at his phone than the screen","Interest, Enthusiasm"],["Skillfulness and sensitivity in dealing with others or difficult issues","She handled the awkward situation with such tact that no one even realized there had been a problem.","Insensitivity, Rudeness"],["Plentiful","The garden was so abundant with vegetables that even the neighbors started leaving zucchini on each other’s doorsteps","Scarce, Insufficient"],["Capable of working successfully, realistic, doable","His plan to build a fort out of pillows and blankets was not only viable but also a masterpiece in engineering","Unworkable, Impractical"],["Contempt, the feeling that someone or something is worthless","He looked at the burnt toast with such scorn that you’d think it had personally insulted him.","Admiration, Respect"],["Misbehave, disobey","His decision to transgress the “No dessert before dinner” rule resulted in the sneakiest midnight ice cream raid ever","Obey, Comply"],["A comparison between two things","Comparing his bad haircut to a mop was an analogy that perfectly captured the disaster","Difference, Contrast"],["A reason for disagreeing","His only objection to the plan was that it didn’t include any snacks—and that was a dealbreaker.","Agreement, Consent"],["To interpret in a particular way","He construed her silence as agreement, but little did he know, she was just thinking about pizza","Misunderstand, Confuse"],["Obtain, acquire","He managed to procure front-row tickets to the concert, a feat that felt like winning the lottery","Lose, Forfeit"],["To bring to mind","The smell of fresh-baked cookies evoked memories of childhood","Suppress, Forget"],["Portrayal, illustration","The artist’s depiction of a cat playing the piano was so realistic, it almost seemed like the cat could play Mozart","Misrepresentation, Distortion"],["A difficulty, problem, or responsibility","Carrying his little brother on his shoulders all day at the amusement park was both a joy and a burden","Relief, Aid"],["A memory; the act of remembering","His recollection of the event was a little fuzzy, but he clearly remembered the giant cake at the end.","Forgetfulness, Amnesia"],["Confusion or disorder","The tumult in the cafeteria was so loud, it sounded like a herd of elephants had taken over lunch.","Peace, Order"],["Admit that something is true after first denying it","After hours of debate, he finally conceded that pineapple on pizza wasn’t that bad","Deny, Refute"]],[["Manner, attitude, appearance","His cheerful demeanor was so infectious that even the grumpy cat started to smile—well, almost","Dullness, Hostility"],["The act of leaving one’s own country","The emigration of penguins from Antarctica to a warmer beach resort was the talk of the animal kingdom","Immigration, Arrival"],["Angry, furious","He became irate when he found out someone had eaten his last slice of pizza—revenge was inevitable","Calm, Peaceful"],["Unconfirmed, subject to change","Their tentative plans for a beach trip were quickly canceled when they realized they didn’t have enough sunscreen","Definite, Certain"],["Only; just","He merely wanted a snack, but ended up devouring the entire cake","Significantly, Considerably"],["To trick or mislead someone","He deceived his little brother into believing that broccoli was just “green candy,” but the taste gave it away","Honest, Inform"],["Unimportant, insignificant","Arguing over who gets the front seat seemed trifling compared to the fact that they were late for the concert","Significant, Important"],["Complicated or confusing","The school’s labyrinthine hallways made it feel like they needed a map and a compass just to find the cafeteria","Simple, Straightforward"],["1) Weak, disabled 2) In a run-down state, decayed","The decrepit old house creaked so much, it sounded like it was telling ghost stories to itself","Sturdy, New"],["To confirm, to verify","The detective corroborated the suspect’s alibi with security footage of him happily eating","Contradict, Disprove"],["Stubbornness, unwilling to change","His obstinacy about not asking for directions turned a 10-minute trip into a 2-hour adventure","Flexibility, Open-mindedness"],["Imprisonment, captivity","The dog’s brief confinement in the backyard felt like a lifetime, and the dramatic escape plan began at once","Freedom, Release"],["Boredom, dullness, lack of variety","The monotony of online meetings was only broken by the occasional appearance of a surprise cat on screen","Excitement, Variety"],["Treat with disrespect","The teacher reminded students not to degrade each other, even during competitive games of dodgeball","Respect, Honor"],["A situation in which a difficult choice has to be made between 2 or more alternatives","He faced a true dilemma: whether to spend his last dollar on ice cream or save it for tomorrow’s lunch","Solution, Certainty"],["Traditional, accepted, mainstream, standard","Wearing a suit to a pool party was far from conventional, but at least he looked sharp in the water","Unorthodox, Unconventional"],["Increase or grow rapidly","His collection of quirky hats began to proliferate after he discovered a store that sold hats shaped like food","Decrease, Dwindle"],["Concerned with beauty or the appreciation of beauty","Her aesthetic sense was so strong that she could turn even the most ordinary room into a work of art","Unattractive, Plain"],["Important; famous","The prominent scientist was so famous that even aliens might recognize him if they came to Earth","Obscure, Unimportant"],["Difficult to carry or move","The unwieldy box of art supplies was so large that it looked like it was trying to move him, not the other way around","Manageable, Convenient"],["Done by only one person or group, without the agreement of others","He unilaterally decided that every meeting should now involve cake, which no one objected to in the","Jointly, Collaboratively"],["To trigger, spark, or activate; to excite","The surprise visit from the puppy stimulated a wave of energy in the office that lasted for hours","Suppress, Dull"],["To become less intense or widespread","The storm’s intensity finally began to abate, leaving behind a rainbow and a yard full of soggy shoes","Intensify, Escalate"],["Hard-working","Her diligent study habits paid off when she aced the final exam, making her textbooks proud","Lazy, Negligent"],["To downgrade, to lower in rank or status","After losing the championship, they were relegated to second-tier status, but they vowed to make a comeback.","Promote, Elevate"]],[["To raise doubts or to protest","He demurred when his friends suggested going on a rollercoaster, citing his “strong preference for solid ground.","Agree, Accept"],["New or unusual in an interesting way","His novel idea to combine pizza and sushi was met with skepticism, but surprisingly, it worked","Common, Traditional"],["Existing in thought or as an idea but not having a physical or concrete existence; conceptual","His abstract painting looked like a mix of colors thrown together, but he insisted it represented “the chaos of the universe","Concrete, Tangible"],["Undeveloped, nonfunctional","The vestigial tail of the ancient creature was still visible in the fossil, though it no longer served any purpose","Developed, Functional"],["Obsessed with something","He was so preoccupied with beating his high score that he didn’t notice the cat sitting on the keyboard","Indifferent, Unconcerned"],["Hopeful and confident about the future","Despite the dark clouds, he remained optimistic that the picnic wouldn’t be rained out—he even packed sunglasses","Pessimistic, Hopeless"],["The act of remembering something; a memory","The old photo album brought back vivid remembrances of summer vacations and ice cream on the beach","Forgetfulness, Amnesia"],["To keep, to hold on to","He tried to retain his composure during the surprise quiz, but the panic was evident in his wide eyes","Lose, Release"],["Easily influenced or harmed by something; vulnerable","He was susceptible to flattery, so his friends always told him he was the best to get him to pay for lunch","Resistant, Immune"],["Difficult, exhausting","Climbing the mountain was so","Easy, Effortless"],["Magic, charm, fascination","The forest was filled with such enchantment that it felt like stepping into a fairy tale, with birds singing in harmony","Repulsion, Dullness"],["Prepared to obey others, submissive, less important","The butler’s subservient attitude was clear as he quietly followed every command without question","Dominant, Independent"],["Based on experience rather than theory or pure logic","The scientist’s empirical data, gathered through years of experiments, spoke louder than any theory could","Theoretical, Hypothetical"],["Unfriendly, threatening","The normally peaceful cat became hostile when someone tried to steal her favorite toy—she hissed like a lion","Friendly, Welcoming"],["To make widely known, to publicize","The new company policy was promulgated so thoroughly that even the janitor knew about the email etiquette rules","Suppress, Conceal"],["To make law, to put into practice (a belief, idea, or suggestion)","The government enacted new laws to protect the endangered species, ensuring they wouldn’t disappear","Repeal, Abolish"],["Miserable, hopeless, awful","The conditions in the abandoned building were abject, with broken windows and crumbling walls","Thriving, Prosperous"],["To use up, to consume","After expending all his energy running the marathon, he collapsed at the finish line and refused to move for an hour","Conserve, Save"],["Giving in to or complying with the requests of others","After hours of begging, she finally became yielding and allowed her little brother to play video games first.","Stubborn, Resistant"],["Embarrassing, shameful","His ignominious fall during the talent show was caught on camera and played on repeat for days","Glorious, Honorable"],["Showing a lack of experience, wisdom, or judgment","His naive belief that he could fix his car with just duct tape and optimism didn’t last long","Worldly, Experienced"],["Something that is bought or obtained, an act of purchase","His latest acquisition, a rare comic book, quickly became the prized possession of his collection","Loss, Forfeiture"],["Wealthy","The affluent neighborhood was full of large mansions, each with perfectly manicured lawns and luxury cars in the driveway","Poor, Impoverished"],["1) Strengthen 2) Combine or unite","The company decided to consolidate its departments, combining marketing and sales into one powerhouse team","Separate, Weaken"],["Very religious or spiritual","The pious monk spent his days in quiet prayer, finding peace in his simple, devoted life.","Irreligious, Secular"]],[["Collection or sum total","The aggregate of all his birthday gifts was impressive—especially the giant stuffed giraffe that wouldn’t fit through the door","Individual, Fragment"],["Disorganized, forgetful","His scatterbrained approach to packing meant he showed up to the beach with three pairs of socks but no swimsuit","Organized, Focused"],["To have an intense feeling of longing for something","After weeks of salad, he yearned for a cheeseburger like a desert yearns for rain.","Dislike, Reject"],["Complete or perfect, having a high degree of skill","She was the consummate chess player, planning her moves ten steps ahead while her opponent was still figuring out where to sit.","Incomplete, Imperfect"],["To support","The celebrity endorsed the new shoe brand, and suddenly everyone wanted to wear them—even though they looked like bananas","Oppose, Reject"],["To find (something) out for certain","He had to ascertain whether his dog really ate his homework or if it was just an excuse—spoiler: it was both.","Ignore, Overlook"],["Involving a lot of effort, difficult","The onerous task of cleaning the garage took so long that he considered turning it into a new room instead","Easy, Simple"],["Fair-minded, not influenced by personal feelings","The judge remained objective throughout the debate, even though one side had cookies as a bribe","Biased, Subjective"],["To hope to achieve something or be successful","He aspired to become a world-famous chef, but for now, his specialty was burning toast","Settle, Neglect"],["No longer produced or used; out","His old flip phone was so","Modern, Current"],["Arousing angry or violent feelings","His inflammatory comment about pineapple on pizza sparked a fiery debate that nearly tore the group apart","Calming, Soothing"],["A view of or attitude towards a situation or event; a general feeling or opinion","The general sentiment in the room was that cats were better than dogs, but the lone dog lover refused to back down","Indifference, Apathy"],["Honesty","His candor during the meeting was refreshing—he wasn’t afraid to say the project was a mess and needed fixing","Deceit, Dishonesty"],["Excessively concerned with material possessions or money","His materialistic obsession with buying the latest gadgets meant he owned five smartwatches—but only had one wrist","Spiritual, Minimalist"],["A dislike or unfair opinion (of someone) that is not based on reason or actual experience","His prejudice against pineapple on pizza was so strong that he refused to try it, despite everyone’s pleas","Fairness, Impartiality"],["Clearly separate and different","The distinct sound of the ice cream truck was enough to make every kid in the neighborhood drop what they were doing and run","Similar, Indistinct"],["Respect","He treated his grandmother with deference, always listening carefully to her stories and following her advice.","Disrespect, Disregard"],["Large in amount or scale","His extensive collection of hats was so large that he needed a separate room just to store them all","Limited, Small"],["1) To force the acceptance of something 2) To cause inconvenience to someone","He didn’t want to impose on his friend by asking for a ride, but the bus stop was ten miles away","Relieve, Lift"],["Having the ability to speak fluently and persuasively","His ability to articulate his thoughts clearly made him the","Inarticulate, Mumbled"],["Original and pure; not spoiled or worn from use","The pristine condition of the rare comic book made it worth more than his entire savings","Dirty, Worn"],["A porch or balcony","They spent the afternoon lounging on the veranda, sipping lemonade and enjoying the view of the garden","Interior, Indoors"],["Unusual, uncommon","His atypical approach to baking involved using chili peppers in cupcakes, which had a surprisingly spicy reception","Typical, Common"],["To bring under domination or control, to conquer","The villain’s plan was to subjugate the world with an army of robots, but his cat kept knocking over the blueprints.","Liberate, Free"],["Everywhere, universal","Cell phones have become so ubiquitous that you can’t walk five feet without seeing someone staring at one.","Rare, Scarce"]],[["A noisy argument or disagreement","Their altercation over who got the last slice of pizza was so loud that even the neighbors started voting on the winner","Agreement, Harmony"],["Strong and healthy, durable","The robust tree withstood the storm, while everything else in the yard, including his hat, blew away","Weak, Fragile"],["To damage or weaken the authority of an established system","The rebellious student tried to subvert the school’s dress code by wearing a neon-green tuxedo","Support, Strengthen"],["Exaggerated, sensationalized, or overemotional","His melodramatic reaction to losing a game of cards made it seem like he’d just lost a fortune, not just a deck of cards","Calm, Subdued"],["An excess supply of something","After the party, there was such a glut of cupcakes that even the ants got tired of them","Shortage, Scarcity"],["Hatred, dislike","His antipathy towards spiders was so strong that he wouldn’t even stay in a room with a picture of one.","Affection, Fondness"],["Dangerous","The perilous climb up the mountain was made worse by the fact that they forgot to pack any snacks","Safe, Secure"],["1) Origin or beginning 2) An idea or concept","The conception of the new app came to him while eating ice cream, proving that dessert really does inspire greatness","End, Conclusion"],["Rest, relaxation","He found a rare moment of repose in the hammock, until the kids discovered him and turned it into a swing","Activity, Agitation"],["To create difficulties for someone or something, resulting in delay","The giant snowstorm impeded their journey, forcing them to","Assist, Facilitate"],["A combination of statements or ideas that are opposed to one another; inconsistency","His claim that he loved exercising was a contradiction to his habit of napping during workout time","Consistency, Agreement"],["Having an excessively critical point of view; disapproving","His judgmental comments about everyone’s outfits made it clear that he thought himself the fashion police","Open-minded, Accepting"],["Depressing, gloomy","The weather was so dismal that even the usually cheerful birds stayed silent in their nests","Cheerful, Bright"],["Open to more than one interpretation; unclear","His ambiguous answer to whether he liked pineapple on pizza left everyone confused—was it a yes or a no?","Clear, Definite"],["Difficult to control or predict because of unusual behavior","The wayward kite zigzagged across the sky, making it impossible to predict where it would land—or if it would ever come down","Predictable, Obedient"],["1) A conclusion that can be drawn from something 2) A consequence or result","The implication of skipping his homework was clear: extra chores on the weekend","Explicitness, Clarification"],["To bring into effective action","The team deployed their secret weapon in the water balloon fight, a giant slingshot that could launch balloons over the fence","Withdraw, Recall"],["Believability, authority","His credibility as a chef skyrocketed after he won the local cooking competition with his famous chocolate mousse","Doubt, Untrustworthiness"],["Overly satisfied or pleased with oneself","His complacent attitude after winning one game made him underestimate his next opponent, who won with ease","Ambitious, Motivated"],["To summon, to call together","The principal convoked the students for an emergency assembly to discuss the mysterious disappearance of all the cafeteria cookies","Disperse, Dismiss"],["Making fun of someone or something in a cruel way","His mocking imitation of the teacher’s voice got a few laughs, but it also earned him a detention","Respectful, Kind"],["The possibility or likelihood of some future event occurring","The prospect of summer vacation kept him going through the final weeks of school, even with a mountain of homework","Impossibility, Unlikelihood"],["Friendly","Despite the breakup, their parting was surprisingly amicable, with no hard feelings and even a few shared laughs","Hostile, Unfriendly"],["Someone or something that came before","His predecessor left big shoes to fill, but he was confident he could lead the team just as well","Successor, Descendant"],["To discourage (someone) from doing something","The sign “Beware of Dog” was enough to deter anyone from entering the yard, even though the dog was a tiny poodle","Encourage, Motivate"]],[["Anger or annoyance","His indignation was obvious when he discovered his favorite snack was missing, and the culprit was his own dog","Calmness, Contentment"],["To restrict or restrain, to put in chains","The strict rules fettered his creativity, making it impossible to express himself freely in art class","Free, Release"],["Stiff, firm, unchangeable","His rigid schedule allowed no room for spontaneous ice cream breaks, much to the dismay of his friends","Flexible, Adaptable"],["To grow, to develop","She worked hard to cultivate a love of reading in her children by filling the house with books","Neglect, Abandon"],["Young, childish, immature","His juvenile sense of humor made everyone roll their eyes, especially when he pulled out the whoopee cushion","Mature, Adult"],["A sudden, violent, irregular movement of the body","His attempt to dance looked more like a series of convulsions, but at least he was having fun","Calmness, Stillness"],["To plan or invent by careful thought","They devised an elaborate plan to surprise their friend, which involved cake, balloons, and a marching band","Improvise, Forget"],["To imprison someone against their will","The villain planned to immure the hero in a tower, but the hero had other ideas—like escaping through the window","Release, Liberate"],["To make someone anxious or unsettled; to disturb","The creepy noises coming from the attic perturbed him so much that he slept with the lights on","Calm, Soothe"],["Care or concern for someone or something","His grandmother’s constant solicitude meant she was always asking if he’d eaten enough or needed a sweater","Indifference, Neglect"],["Spreading widely throughout an area or group of people","The pervasive smell of freshly baked cookies filled the entire house, drawing everyone to the kitchen.","Limited, Contained"],["Cruel and abusive government or rule","The king’s tyranny led to a revolt as people demanded freedom from his unfair laws.","Freedom, Democracy"],["Anxious or fearful that something bad or unpleasant will happen","He was apprehensive about skydiving, but once he jumped, the fear turned into excitement","Confident, Relaxed"],["1) A condition or requirement in a legal document 2) The act of providing services or resources","The contract had a provision that allowed them to cancel anytime, which gave them peace of mind","Refusal, Neglect"],["Showing a rude lack of respect","His insolent remark to the teacher earned him a trip to the principal’s office","Polite, Respectful"],["General agreement","After much debate, the group reached a consensus to order pizza for dinner.","Disagreement, Division"],["Disagreement between people","The discord between the two teams was so intense that even the referees couldn’t calm things down","Harmony, Agreement"],["To add to (something) in a way that enhances or completes it","The spicy salsa complemented the mild guacamole perfectly, creating a delicious balance of flavors.","Contrast, Clash"],["To cause (someone) to feel embarrassed, ashamed, or humiliated","He was mortified when his phone rang loudly in the middle of the silent library.","Comfort, Praise"],["To disappear or evaporate","The fog dissipated as the sun rose, revealing a clear view of the mountains","Gather, Accumulate"],["A belief or set of beliefs","The school’s doctrine emphasized kindness and respect for all, values they instilled in every student","Ambiguity, Doubt"],["Not able to be understood","His handwriting was so messy that it was completely incomprehensible, leaving everyone guessing what the note","Understandable, Clear"],["To tell someone about something, to give a report of an event","He eagerly recounted the story of his adventure at the amusement park, complete with sound effects and dramatic pauses","Conceal, Hide"],["Unable to produce the intended result","His attempt to fix the leaky faucet with duct tape was inefficacious, and water sprayed everywhere","Effective, Successful"],["One’s opponent or enemy","His adversary in the chess tournament was a fierce competitor, but he managed to win with a clever move","Ally, Friend"]],[["To provide, to supply","The school was endowed with state-of-the-art computers, making every student feel like a tech genius","Deprive, Withdraw"],["To cause surprise or confusion in someone","His ability to solve the Rubik’s Cube in seconds confounded his friends, who were still stuck on step one","Clarify, Enlighten"],["To state a fact or belief confidently and forcefully","She asserted her right to the last piece of cake, declaring it with such conviction that no one dared challenge her","Deny, Question"],["To gradually damage or weaken someone or something","The constant criticism slowly undermined his confidence, making him doubt even his best work","Strengthen, Support"],["A statement or situation that may be true but seems impossible or difficult to understand because it contains two opposite facts or characteristics","It’s a paradox that the more you sleep, the more tired you sometimes feel","Consistency, Certainty"],["Appropriate or suitable in the circumstances","His joke about the rain was apt, especially since everyone had just arrived soaking wet.","Inappropriate, Unsuitable"],["Having the necessary ability, knowledge, or skill to do something successfully","He was a competent mechanic, able to fix anything from a car engine to a squeaky door","Incompetent, Inept"],["The quality of being very unpleasant, unkind, or difficult","The severity of the storm forced everyone to stay indoors and cancel all weekend plans","Gentleness, Softness"],["A feeling of shock and unhappiness","His dismay was evident when he realized the ice cream shop had just run out of his favorite flavor","Joy, Delight"],["To take power or control of something by force or without","The knight attempted to usurp the throne, but his plan was","Relinquish, Surrender"],["Feeling happy and also slightly sad when you think about things that happened in the past","Listening to his old favorite songs made him feel nostalgic for his high school days.","Unsentimental, Forgetful"],["Having a lot of complex patterns or decoration","The ornate chandelier sparkled so much it looked like a piece of art hanging from the ceiling","Simple, Plain"],["A system in which people or things are put at various levels or ranks according to their importance","The office hierarchy was clear, with the boss at the top and the interns scrambling at the bottom","Equality, Disorder"],["Not logical or reasonable","His irrational fear of flying made vacations complicated, especially since he lived on an island","Rational, Logical"],["Talk intended to seem important or threatening but which is not taken seriously and has little effect","His bluster about quitting his job was ignored by everyone—he said it at least once a week","Calmness, Quietness"],["Having a lower or less important position","In the company, the interns were seen as subordinate to the full-time staff, even though they worked just as hard","Superior, Leader"],["Intending to cause harm; evil","The malicious hacker tried to steal everyone’s data, but was stopped by a strong firewall.","Benevolent, Kind"],["To revise, to make changes","They had to amend the report several times before it was finally approved by the boss.","Worsen, Damage"],["To behave according to an expectation or rule","He refused to conform to the office dress code, showing up in bright, mismatched outfits every day","Rebel, Deviate"],["To advertise or praise something (often to sell it)","The salesman touted the benefits of his product so much that it started to sound too good to be true","Criticize, Disparage"],["To spread throughout something","The smell of fresh popcorn permeated the theater, making everyone crave a snack.","Contain, Block"],["A series of words said as a magic spell or charm","The wizard muttered an ancient incantation, and suddenly the","Impervious"],["Not able to be influenced, hurt, or damaged","His thick winter coat made him impervious to the cold wind blowing across the mountain","Vulnerable, Permeable"],["1) To cause (a machine or device) to operate 2) To cause (someone) to act in a particular way","The switch actuated the alarm system, sending everyone into a panic","Deactivate, Suppress"],["Ability to adapt to many different functions or activities","Her versatility as an athlete meant she excelled at everything from swimming to soccer.","Rigidity, Inflexibility"]],[["To announce officially or publicly","The mayor proclaimed that every Friday would be Free Ice Cream Day, and the entire town cheered","Conceal, Suppress"],["Deep respect","The knight showed obeisance to the queen by kneeling before her and swearing loyalty","Disrespect, Scorn"],["1) Humble, not showy 2) Not large in size or amount","Despite his success, he remained modest, never boasting about his achievements.","Arrogant, Showy"],["To decorate","They adorned the Christmas tree with lights, ornaments, and a star on top","Disfigure, Deface"],["The state or situation of being alone","She found peace in the solitude of the forest, far away from the noise of the city.","Company, Togetherness"],["To use up the supply or resources of","The long hike quickly depleted their water supply, leaving them thirsty and tired.","Replenish, Restore"],["Having or showing serious purpose and determination; formal","The graduation ceremony was solemn, with speeches about the future and a few tears.","Joyful, Lighthearted"],["A person who supports an idea, plan, or cause","He was a strong proponent of renewable energy, always promoting solar and wind power","Opponent, Critic"],["Sharp; highly developed (usually the senses)","Her keen sense of smell allowed her to detect the faintest hint of cookies baking.","Dull, Blunt"],["To surround and cover completely","The waves engulfed the small boat, leaving it barely visible beneath the water.","Release, Free"],["To go in different directions from the same point, to become different","The paths diverged in the woods, and they had to choose which one to follow.","Converge, Unite"],["Extremely dirty, poor, and unpleasant","The abandoned house was squalid, with broken windows","Clean, Pristine"],["Imagined or suggested but not necessarily real or true","The professor posed a hypothetical question about time travel, sparking a lively debate.","Actual, Real"],["Urgent or needing to be dealt with immediately","The pressing deadline forced him to work late into the night","Minor, Unimportant"],["A request for money, information, or help","The charity sent out a solicitation for donations to help families in need","Refusal, Denial"],["Interfere in something that is not one’s concern","His little brother loved to meddle in his business, always snooping around and asking too many questions","Ignore, Overlook"],["1) Rough, not smooth 2) Rude or offensive in manner or speech","The sandpaper was coarse to the touch, perfect for smoothing out the rough wood.","Smooth, Refined"],["To criticize or express disapproval with someone","His mother reproached him for not finishing his homework before going out with friends.","Praise, Approve"],["1) To put something completely under a liquid 2) To involve someone completely in an activity","She immersed herself in the book, losing track of time as she read for hours.","Remove, Withdraw"],["Power and influence (especially in politics or business)","The CEO’s clout in the industry meant that everyone listened when he spoke.","Weakness, Powerlessness"],["To make something that is already bad worse","His decision to skip studying only exacerbated his stress when the exam arrived.","Alleviate, Improve"],["Doubtful","He was dubious about the claim that eating chocolate could help you lose weight.","Certain, Sure"],["Possibly true, able to be believed, reasonable","His explanation for why he was late was plausible, though still a bit suspicious.","Implausible, Unlikely"],["A belief or idea","The notion that he could finish the entire pizza by himself seemed ambitious but possible.","Reality, Fact"],["Able to judge something fairly","The judge was impartial, weighing both sides of the argument equally before making","Biased, Prejudiced"]],[["A long strip or area of something","The farmer cut a wide swath through the field, leaving a neat row of wheat behind him.","Fragment, Patch"],["To try an activity in a casual way","He likes to dabble in painting, though he’s not ready to call himself an artist just yet.","Specialize, Master"],["Sincere and serious","His earnest apology made it clear he truly regretted his mistake","Insincere, Flippant"],["Life, energy, and strength","The dancer’s vitality was contagious, filling the entire room with excitement.","Lethargy, Weakness"],["To imitate or copy (someone’s actions or words)","The parrot loved to mimic his owner, repeating everything in a high-pitched voice.","Differ, Originate"],["1) To make someone troubled or nervous 2) To campaign for something in public","The loud noises outside began to agitate the baby, who started to cry.","Calm, Soothe"],["Likely to succeed or be effective in real circumstances, relating to actual experience rather than knowledge only","His practical solution to the problem saved time and effort, proving his experience was valuable","Impractical, Theoretical"],["Suggesting something unpleasant will happen","The dark clouds looked ominous, hinting at a storm on the way","Bright, Promising"],["1) Control over a country or people 2) The land that belongs to a ruler","The king’s dominion stretched across vast lands, but his people lived peacefully.","Submission, Subordination"],["A false display, an attempt to deceive","Under the pretense of being friendly, he gathered information for his own gain.","Honesty, Sincerity"],["Thinking only of oneself; self-centered","His egocentric attitude made him forget that his friends also had opinions and feelings.","Altruistic, Selfless"],["To make full use of (a resource), to use (a person) in an unfair or","The company was criticized for exploiting its workers, offering","Support, Nurture"],["To consist of or to be made up of","The team comprises players from five different countries, making it truly international.","Exclude, Lack"],["A dangerous, difficult, or otherwise unfortunate situation","The plight of the stranded hikers was worsened by the sudden snowstorm","Blessing, Advantage"],["To be a typical example of something","His work ethic exemplified what it means to be a dedicated student.","Misrepresent, Distort"],["Very important (in reference to a decision or event)","The signing of the peace treaty was a momentous event in the nation’s history.","Trivial, Unimportant"],["To continue to be heard; to echo repeatedly","The sound of the bell reverberated through the empty halls, filling the space with a low hum.","Mute, Silence"],["Behaving or feeling as a father does toward his child","His paternal instincts kicked in when he saw the child lost in the store, and he immediately offered help.","Maternal, Distant"],["To express sadness and regret about something","She lamented the loss of her favorite necklace, which had sentimental value.","Celebrate, Rejoice"],["The process by which someone tries to end a disagreement by helping the two sides to talk about and agree on a solution","The mediation between the two companies helped resolve the dispute without going to court","Dispute, Argument"],["Someone who has a great desire to possess money and hates to spend it","The old miser refused to part with a single coin, even though he had more money than he could ever use","Spender, Philanthropist"],["Bending or able to be bent easily; not stiff; flexible","The gymnast’s supple body allowed her to perform moves most people could only dream of","Rigid, Stiff"],["Not aware of what is happening around you","He was so engrossed in his book that he was oblivious to the chaos happening around him.","Aware, Attentive"],["Silent and unpleasant; depressed; gloomy","After losing the game, he sat in sullen silence, refusing to talk to anyone","Cheerful, Joyful"],["1) Extremely important or urgent 2) Something that needs to be done immediately","It’s imperative that we finish the project by Friday, or we’ll miss the deadline.","Optional, Unimportant"]],[["To talk about the past with pleasure","They loved to reminisce about their childhood adventures, laughing at all the mischief they used to get into","Forget, Ignore"],["Calm, quiet, and peaceful","The tranquil sound of the river made it the perfect spot to sit and relax with a good book.","Chaotic, Noisy"],["To cut or split into at least two parts","The sword cleaved through the air, cutting the fruit cleanly in two","Unite, Combine"],["An unwillingness to do something","His reluctance to speak in front of the class was clear, as he avoided making eye contact with the teacher.","Willingness, Eagerness"],["A feeling of doubt, uncertainty, or worry about a future event","She had misgivings about signing the contract, feeling uneasy about the terms.","Confidence, Assurance"],["Small in number, often spread over a large area; scarce","The sparse trees in the desert offered little shade from the blazing sun","Dense, Abundant"],["Originator, creator, founder","He was the progenitor of the company, building it from the ground up with just an idea and hard work","Follower, Successor"],["Ridiculous or completely unreasonable","The idea that cats could rule the world seemed absurd, but it still made for a funny movie","Reasonable, Rational"],["An idea or theory on which a statement or action is based; an assumption","The movie’s premise was simple—a superhero who could only use their powers once a day","Conclusion, Reality"],["To examine someone or something very carefully","The jeweler scrutinized the diamond closely to ensure it was flawless.","Overlook, Ignore"],["Added to something else in order to improve it or complete it","The supplemental guide provided additional tips for","Primary, Essential"],["Causing a feeling of sadness","The movie’s poignant ending left everyone in the theater wiping away tears.","Cheerful, Unemotional"],["Not known to many people, difficult to understand","The professor mentioned an obscure historical figure that none of the students had ever heard of.","Famous, Clear"],["Belonging to or inherited from one’s ancestors","The family’s ancestral home had been passed down through generations, filled with history and memories.","Modern, New"],["Fond of company; sociable","His gregarious personality made him the life of every party, always surrounded by friends","Shy, Reserved"],["To use power or the ability to make something happen","The athlete exerted all his strength in the final lap to win the race","Refrain, Withhold"],["Strong, healthy, and full of energy","After a vigorous workout, she felt energized and ready to take on the day","Weak, Lethargic"],["To ask someone sincerely or anxiously to do something","He entreated his friend to forgive him, apologizing over and over.","Demand, Command"],["A state of complete emptiness or destruction","The desolation of the abandoned town was eerie, with empty streets and crumbling buildings.","Liveliness, Joyfulness"],["Famous for something bad","The notorious criminal was finally caught after years of evading the police","Respected, Honored"],["1) To persuade someone to do something 2) To cause something to happen","The doctor induced labor to help the baby be born safely.","Prevent, Dissuade"],["Feeling that one is better or more important than other people","His pompous speech made it clear he thought he was the most important person in the room.","Humble, Modest"],["To criticize someone or something in a way that shows a lack of respect","He disparaged his coworker’s ideas during the meeting, making her feel embarrassed.","Praise, Compliment"],["Complete and in the original state; not damaged","Despite the storm, the house remained intact, with not a single","Broken, Damaged"],["An opinion or judgment","The jury delivered a verdict of “not guilty,” much to the relief of the defendant.","Mistrial, Uncertainty"]],[["Ordinary and dull","His weekend was filled with mundane tasks like laundry and grocery shopping, nothing exciting at all.","Exciting, Extraordinary"],["To encourage an activity or development, to cause something to develop faster","The coach’s pep talk spurred the team to play their best and win the championship","Discourage, Hinder"],["A guard whose job is to stand and keep watch","The sentinel stood at the castle gates, alert for any signs of danger.","Intruder, Offender"],["To make (an idea or feeling) known or understandable to someone; to communicate","He struggled to convey his gratitude, finally settling on a heartfelt thank-you note.","Conceal, Muddle"],["To cause someone or something to be in a particular state","The artist’s skillful painting rendered the scene so lifelike it felt like you could step into it.","Destroy, Diminish"],["To show something clearly, through signs or actions","Her nervousness manifested in her shaky hands as she prepared for the presentation.","Hide, Conceal"],["A continuous sequence; a range","Emotions exist on a continuum, with happiness at one end and sadness at the other.","Fragment, Interruption"],["To correct a wrong","The company offered free repairs to redress the problems caused by their faulty products.","Worsen, Aggravate"],["To emphasize the importance of something","The teacher underscored the importance of studying, reminding students that the final exam was only a week away.","Downplay, Diminish"],["To make someone or something very weak","The long illness enfeebled him so much that even walking across the room was exhausting.","Strengthen, Energize"],["Dislike of someone or something that one feels does not deserve respect","He looked at the broken-down car with disdain, refusing to even consider buying it.","Respect, Admiration"],["To praise someone in order to please him or her","The employee tried to flatter the boss with compliments, hoping to get a promotion.","Criticize, Insult"],["All future generations of people","The founding fathers made decisions that would affect posterity, ensuring freedom for future generations.","Ancestors, Forefathers"],["To strengthen or support; to keep alive","The trees sustained the village by providing food, shelter, and medicine for generations.","Harm, Weaken"],["1) Not mixed with anything else; pure or complete 2) Very large","The sheer size of the mountain left everyone speechless as they began the long climb.","Partial, Mixed"],["To judge the quality or importance of something","The coach carefully assessed each player’s performance before making the final team selection","Ignore, Neglect"],["A person who does skilled work with his or her hands","The artisan crafted beautiful, handmade pottery that was admired by everyone at the market.","Amateur, Novice"],["Not loud, bright, noticeable, or obvious","The subtle hint of lemon in the dish added a refreshing flavor without overpowering the other ingredients","Obvious, Blatant"],["To refuse to accept something or someone; to reject","He repudiated the false accusations, providing evidence that proved his innocence.","Accept, Embrace"],["To follow a route that is not straight or direct","The river meandered through the valley, twisting and turning before reaching the ocean","Rush, Go straight"],["Successful in producing the intended results","His effectual leadership helped the company grow faster than anyone expected.","Ineffective, Useless"],["Very small in amount or number","The meager portion of food left everyone still feeling hungry after dinner","Abundant, Plentiful"],["Boring, slow, and tiring","Sorting through the paperwork was a tedious task, but it had to be done.","Exciting, Engaging"],["To carefully measure or adjust","The technician calibrated the machine to ensure it worked","Disorganize, Neglect"],["Powerful, persuasive, or effective","The potent medicine worked quickly, relieving her headache in minutes","Weak, Ineffective"]],[["Providing the right conditions for something to happen or exist; to help bring about","The quiet library was conducive to studying, allowing him to focus without distractions.","Inhibitive, Unfavorable"],["Tending to keep feelings or thoughts private; quiet","She was reserved during the meeting, listening carefully but not sharing her opinions.","Outgoing, Expressive"],["A mixture of different things","The chef prepared a medley of vegetables, blending flavors from around the world.","Uniformity, Similarity"],["1) To support an idea 2) A person who publicly supports an idea","She is a strong advocate for animal rights, often speaking at rallies to raise awareness.","Oppose, Critic"],["To move with a smooth, wavelike motion","The flags undulated in the breeze, creating a mesmerizing display","Stiffen, Stabilize"],["1) The great size or importance of something 2) The extent or degree of something","The magnitude of the earthquake was so great that buildings across the city were damaged","Insignificance, Smallness"],["To make someone more powerful or important","The company’s new advertising campaign was designed to aggrandize its CEO as a visionary leader.","Belittle, Diminish"],["To hit someone or something repeatedly","The boxer pummeled his opponent with a series of rapid punches, securing his victory.","Pat, Soothe"],["Easily frightened; shy","The timid puppy hid behind the couch whenever a loud noise startled him","Bold, Confident"],["An unfair personal opinion that influences your judgment","His bias against certain groups clouded his ability to make fair decisions.","Fairness, Impartiality"],["To improve something by making small changes","The artist refined her painting, adding details that made it more realistic","Deteriorate, Worsen"],["To swing back and forth","The fan oscillated, cooling different parts of the room as it moved","Stabilize, Steady"],["Respect and admiration for someone","He was held in high esteem by his colleagues for his dedication and hard work.","Disrespect, Contempt"],["To force something or someone out of its usual or original place","The flood displaced many families, forcing them to leave their homes","Settle, Anchor"],["A raised platform in a church from which the preacher speaks","The preacher delivered his sermon from the pulpit, his voice echoing through the church","Floor, Audience"],["Clever, original, and inventive (in reference to a person)","His ingenious solution to the problem impressed everyone in the room","Unimaginative, Ordinary"],["To be the parts that form something","The committee constitutes members from various departments to ensure fair representation.","Dismantle, Ruin"],["Impossible to satisfy","His insatiable appetite for knowledge meant he was always reading or asking questions.","Satisfied, Content"],["The power to make one’s own decisions","She left the company of her own volition, deciding it was time to pursue new opportunities.","Coercion, Compulsion"],["To like or enjoy something","He relished every bite of the delicious meal, savoring the flavors.","Dislike, Detest"],["To make (an action or process) possible or easier","The new software will facilitate communication between the teams, making collaboration more efficient.","Hinder, Block"],["The level or point at which something starts","They were on the threshold of a scientific breakthrough, with only a few more experiments to go.","End, Conclusion"],["To make changes in something in order to improve it","The government promised to reform the education system to provide better opportunities for students.","Worsen, Deteriorate"],["To make a facial expression that","He sneered at his rival, showing","Smile, Praise"],["1) Intense, extreme 2) Requiring deep thought","His speech left a profound impact on the audience, moving many to tears.","Superficial, Shallow"]]],"iv":[[["Difficult to understand","The professor’s abstruse explanation of quantum mechanics left many students confused","Clear, Simple"],["Appropriate, inclined","His apt remark about the situation perfectly captured everyone’s feelings","Inappropriate, Unfitting"],["To coax","She managed to cajole her friend into joining her at the party, despite initial reluctance","Dissuade, Discourage"],["Succinct","His compendious summary of the meeting saved everyone from reading the full report","Lengthy, Wordy"],["To agree","The scientists concurred on the findings, confirming the accuracy of the results.","Disagree, Oppose"],["To list, explain","The speaker delineated the steps to solving the problem, making it easy for everyone to follow.","Confuse, Distort"],["To stray from the subject at hand","He started to discuss his weekend plans but quickly digressed into a story about his dog.","Stay focused, Stay on topic"],["To clarify","The teacher elucidated the complex math problem, making it easier for the students to understand","Obscure, Confuse"],["Involved in an argument or conflict","The neighbors were embroiled in a heated argument about the","Exclude, Disengage"],["Based on observation and experiment (not theory)","The scientist’s empirical data provided strong evidence for the new hypothesis.","Theoretical, Hypothetical"],["To list","He enumerated the reasons for his decision, making it clear why he chose that option.","Generalize, Simplify"],["Representative example","Her dedication to her work epitomizes what it means to be a committed employee.","Exception, Deviation"],["Ambiguous","His equivocal response left everyone wondering what he really meant","Clear, Definite"],["Representative example","The student’s essay was an exemplar of excellent writing, used as a model for others.","Counterexample, Outlier"],["To encourage","The coach exhorted his team to give their best effort in the final game","Discourage, Deter"],["Useful","The expedient solution helped resolve the issue quickly, though it wasn’t ideal.","Useless, Impractical"],["To understand","She couldn’t fathom why her friend would act that way, leaving her puzzled.","Misunderstand, Misinterpret"],["Evident, obvious","His flagrant disregard for the rules led to his immediate disqualification from the competition","Subtle, Hidden"],["Flushed, flowery","His florid speech was filled with elaborate metaphors, making it hard to follow.","Plain, Simple"],["Inappropriateness, discrepancy","The incongruity of her casual outfit at the formal event was hard to ignore.","Harmony, Consistency"],["Impossible to express in words","The beauty of the sunset was ineffable, leaving everyone speechless.","Expressible, Describable"],["Implicit suggestion","His speech was full of innuendos, hinting at his true feelings without directly stating them.","Direct statement, Overt"],["Concise","His laconic reply, a simple “yes,” left little room for further discussion.","Verbose, Wordy"],["Clear, easily understood","The instructions were so lucid that even beginners had no trouble following them","Confusing, Obscure"],["Vague","His plans were so nebulous that no one could figure out what he actually intended to do.","Clear, Precise"]],[["Subtle difference","There was a nuance in his tone that suggested he was upset, though he didn’t say it outright.","Obviousness"],["Clear example","Her behavior was a paradigm of professionalism.","Exception"],["Babble","The child’s prattle went on for hours without making much sense.","Silence"],["Formal declaration","The judge’s pronouncement ended the heated debate in the courtroom.","Inquiry"],["Supporter","He was a strong proponent of renewable energy solutions.","Opponent"],["Lacking imagination, dull","His prosaic speech failed to inspire the audience.","Imaginative, Creative"],["Defense, counterargument","The lawyer's rebuttal weakened the opposing counsel's case.","Agreement"],["To reject, take back","The witness recanted her earlier testimony after realizing it was incorrect.","Confirm"],["To reject","She repudiated the accusations made against her.","Accept"],["To annul, retract","The company rescinded the offer after a background check revealed discrepancies.","Uphold, Grant"],["Elegant speech or writing","The politician’s rhetoric was filled with persuasive and convincing points.","Plain speaking"],["To examine carefully","The auditor scrutinized the financial records for any discrepancies.","Overlook"],["A comparison using 'like' or 'as'","The poet used a simile to describe her smile as bright as the sun.","Dissimilarity"],["Irrelevant, digressive","His comment was tangential to the topic being discussed.","Relevant"],["Extensive written argument","She published a treatise on the environmental effects of deforestation.","Essay"],["Wordy, long-winded","His verbose explanation made the simple concept difficult to follow.","Concise"],["Air, feeling","The old mansion had an eerie aura that made everyone uncomfortable.","Absence of atmosphere"],["Pompous, inflated","His bombastic remarks made it hard for anyone to take him seriously.","Modest"],["Cheerful, floating","Her buoyant personality made her the life of the party.","Depressed"],["Insensitive","His callous disregard for others' feelings left everyone shocked.","Compassionate"],["Irritable, argumentative","The cantankerous neighbor complained about everything.","Agreeable"],["Fickle, unpredictable","The weather in the mountains is notoriously capricious, changing without warning.","Predictable"],["Bitter, sarcastic","Her caustic remarks stung even though they were meant as a joke.","Gentle, Kind"],["Sociable, lively","The convivial atmosphere at the party made everyone feel welcome.","Reserved"],["Openly emotional","She is very demonstrative, always expressing her emotions clearly and without hesitation.","Reserved, Restrained"]],[["Sad, depressed","After the loss of his job, he felt despondent for weeks.","Elated"],["Shy, lacking self-confidence","The diffident student hesitated to speak in front of the class.","Confident"],["Disappointed, defeated","She was discomfited by the sudden change in plans.","Comforted"],["Disenchantment, disappointment","The harsh reality of life led to her disillusionment with politics.","Idealism"],["Unemotional, impartial","The judge remained dispassionate throughout the heated trial.","Emotional"],["Joyful, thrilled","He was elated when he received the acceptance letter from his dream university.","Despondent"],["To bring about, stir up","The old song evoked memories of her childhood.","Suppress"],["Well-suited, happy","His felicitous choice of words made his speech very moving.","Inappropriate"],["Sad, abandoned","The forlorn dog waited by the door for its owner to return.","Cheerful"],["Courage in adversity","She showed great fortitude in the face of overwhelming challenges.","Weakness"],["Commotion, anger","The politician's comments caused a furor among the public.","Calm"],["Overly dramatic or emotional","Her histrionic outburst made everyone uncomfortable.","Subdued"],["Simple and tranquil","They spent a week at an idyllic cabin by the lake.","Chaotic"],["Rash, impulsive","His impetuous decision to quit his job surprised everyone.","Cautious"],["Angry, enraged","The customer became irate when his complaint was ignored.","Calm"],["Tired, bored, lacking enthusiasm","After years of working in the same job, she felt jaded and unmotivated.","Energetic"],["Cheerful, humorous","His jocular personality made him popular at parties.","Serious"],["Cheerful and friendly","She was in a jovial mood after hearing the good news.","Melancholy"],["Overly sentimental","He became maudlin after a few drinks, reminiscing about his past.","Unemotional"],["Bleak, sad","There was a melancholy atmosphere at the funeral.","Jovial"],["Fickle, changeable","Her mercurial temperament made it difficult to predict her reactions.","Stable"],["Gloomy, sullen","He became morose after losing his job.","Cheerful"],["Easily irritated","She became peevish when things didn’t go her way.","Easy-going"],["A strong preference","He has a penchant for collecting rare stamps.","Dislike"],["Done without care or interest","His perfunctory handshake showed that he wasn’t truly interested in making a connection.","Thorough, Diligent"]],[["Irritable, easily annoyed","The petulant child threw a tantrum when he didn’t get his way.","Good-natured"],["Intense, significant","Her speech left a profound impact on everyone who heard it.","Superficial"],["Inclination, tendency","He has a propensity to overthink even simple decisions.","Disinclination"],["Offensive, disgusting","The smell coming from the garbage was utterly repugnant.","Pleasant"],["Emotionally reserved","She remained reticent during the discussion, keeping her thoughts to herself.","Talkative"],["Cheerfully optimistic","Despite the challenges, she remained sanguine about her future.","Pessimistic"],["Comfort, consolation","He sought solace in his friends after the breakup.","Distress"],["Bleak, gloomy","The somber mood in the room reflected the tragic news.","Bright"],["Moody, unpredictable","Her temperamental nature made it difficult to work with her.","Stable"],["Apprehension, fear","She approached the stage with trepidation, unsure of how the audience would react.","Confidence"],["Aggressive, bad-tempered","The truculent attitude of the customer made the situation worse.","Friendly"],["Felt indirectly through another's experience","She felt vicarious excitement watching her friend perform.","Direct"],["Anger, rage","The wrath of the storm left a trail of destruction.","Calm"],["Eagerness, readiness","She accepted the invitation with alacrity.","Reluctance"],["Inactive","The volcano had been dormant for decades before erupting again.","Active"],["Enthusiastic, lively","His ebullient personality made him the life of every gathering.","Depressed"],["Calmness, composure","She faced the chaos with equanimity, staying calm throughout.","Anxiety"],["Robust, sturdy","The hardy plants survived the harsh winter conditions.","Weak"],["Lazy, avoiding activity","His indolent behavior prevented him from achieving his goals.","Active"],["Dull, boring","The presentation was so insipid that half the audience fell asleep.","Exciting"],["To provoke, start","His comments instigated a heated argument among the group.","Suppress"],["To call forth, appeal to","The lawyer invoked a precedent to strengthen her case.","Revoke"],["Lacking energy, lethargic","His lackadaisical attitude towards his work frustrated his colleagues.","Energetic"],["Lazy person","The laggard in the group held up the completion of the project.","Leader"],["Lacking energy; slow and relaxed","After a long, hot day, she lay languid on the couch, too tired to move.","Energetic, Vigorous"]],[["Languid, sluggish","She felt listless after staying up all night.","Energetic"],["Short period of calm","There was a lull in the conversation after the awkward comment.","Commotion"],["To soothe or calm","The mother pacified her crying baby with a lullaby.","Agitate"],["To calm someone down","The manager tried to placate the upset customer with a discount.","Provoke"],["Calm","The placid lake was a perfect spot for relaxation.","Agitated"],["Harsh, rowdy","The raucous crowd made it difficult to hear the speaker.","Quiet"],["To provoke, excite","The leader's speech roused the crowd into action.","Calm"],["Lively, effervescent","Her scintillating performance captivated the audience.","Dull"],["Not moving, inactive","The stagnant water in the pond became a breeding ground for mosquitoes.","Flowing"],["Not moving","The static economy showed no signs of growth.","Dynamic"],["Drowsiness, apathy","After a big meal, he fell into a state of torpor.","Energy"],["Boisterous, unrestrained","The unruly children caused chaos in the classroom.","Disciplined"],["Dull, uninteresting","The conversation was so vapid that he struggled to stay awake.","Exciting"],["Hatred","She abhors violence in any form.","Love"],["Bitter animosity","The acrimony between the two rivals was evident during the debate.","Friendship"],["Friendly","Her amiable personality made her well-liked by everyone.","Unfriendly"],["Friendly","Their divorce was surprisingly amicable, with both parties agreeing on terms.","Hostile"],["Dislike","He had a deep antipathy for dishonesty.","Affection"],["Pleasant","The congenial atmosphere made the party enjoyable for everyone.","Unpleasant"],["Quarrelsome","Her disputatious nature often led to arguments with her friends.","Agreeable"],["Dislike, aversion","He expressed his distaste for the new policy.","Liking"],["Compassionate","She was empathetic towards her friend’s struggles.","Apathetic"],["Alienate","The argument estranged him from his family for years.","Reconcile"],["Demanding, severe","The exacting standards of the program were difficult to meet.","Lenient"],["Friendly and cheerful","His genial smile and warm greeting made everyone feel welcome at the party.","Unfriendly, Hostile"]],[["Meddlesome, interfering","The officious neighbor kept giving unsolicited advice.","Uninvolved"],["Intentional mockery","The comedian's parody of the politician had the audience in stitches.","Tribute"],["Bitter, resentful","Their rancorous relationship was filled with arguments and bitterness.","Amicable"],["Relationship","She had a good rapport with her colleagues, which made working together easier.","Discord"],["A hermit, someone who avoids others","The famous author lived as a recluse for many years.","Socialite"],["Sarcastic imitation","The movie was a satire on modern politics, full of sharp humor.","Seriousness"],["Expressing care or concern, often too much","The solicitous mother hovered over her child, worried about every move.","Indifferent"],["Unintentional","He made an unwitting mistake that led to a series of unfortunate events.","Intentional"],["Yielding, open to suggestions","She was amenable to trying out the new approach at work.","Uncooperative"],["Strive for","She aspired to become a world-class dancer.","Settle"],["Diligent, hardworking","Her assiduous efforts resulted in a successful project.","Lazy"],["To relieve or appease","He tried to assuage his guilt by apologizing.","Aggravate"],["Yielding, submissive","The team was compliant with the new regulations.","Defiant"],["Courageous","The dauntless explorer ventured into uncharted territories.","Fearful"],["Failure","The event was a complete debacle, with nothing going according to plan.","Success"],["To weaken","The illness debilitated him to the point where he could barely stand.","Strengthen"],["To prove wrong","The scientist debunked the popular myth with solid evidence.","Validate"],["Respectful submission","Out of deference to her expertise, they followed her advice.","Defiance"],["Hindrance, impediment","The threat of punishment acted as a deterrent to potential lawbreakers.","Incentive"],["Discouraging","The negative feedback was disheartening, but he continued working hard.","Encouraging"],["To drive away or disprove","She managed to dispel the rumors with a simple explanation.","Confirm"],["Anxiety","There was a sense of disquiet in the room as they waited for the results.","Calm"],["Superficial, effortless","His facile response did not address the complexities of the issue.","Thorough"],["Hopeless, without effect","Their efforts to save the company were ultimately futile.","Effective"],["Brave, heroic behavior; polite attention or respect given by men to women","The knight showed great gallantry by defending the villagers from danger.","Cowardice, Rudeness"]],[["Obstacle, deadlock","The negotiations reached an impasse, with neither side willing to compromise.","Breakthrough"],["Too strong to be defeated","Her indomitable spirit kept her going even when things were tough.","Weak"],["Courageous, fearless","The intrepid adventurer explored the uncharted wilderness.","Cowardly"],["Difficult, trying","The task was so onerous that many employees quit.","Easy"],["Submissive, subservient","His servile attitude towards his boss was noticed by everyone.","Dominant"],["Loyal, not yielding","She remained steadfast in her belief, despite opposition.","Wavering"],["Obedient, yielding","The subservient assistant followed every order without question.","Independent"],["Determined, persistent","Her tenacious efforts finally paid off when she was accepted into the program.","Weak-willed"],["Insignificant, flimsy","His argument was tenuous and failed to convince the jury.","Strong"],["Suffering, distress","The family endured many tribulations during the difficult times.","Joy"],["Striving","Several companies were vying for the lucrative contract.","Ignoring"],["Insightfulness","Her business acumen helped her turn the company into a success.","Ignorance"],["Skillful","She is adept at solving complex problems.","Clumsy"],["Skillful","The surgeon's adroit hands saved the patient.","Inept"],["Study of human beings","He decided to major in anthropology to learn more about ancient cultures.","None"],["Crude, unmannered","His boorish behavior at the dinner offended many guests.","Polite"],["Intellectual","The book is too cerebral for me; I prefer more action-packed stories.","Unintelligent"],["Rude, boorish","The churlish comments upset everyone at the table.","Polite"],["Careful, diligent","She was conscientious in completing her assignments on time.","Careless"],["Sophisticated, urbane","He has a cosmopolitan view, having traveled to many countries.","Provincial"],["Gullibility, tendency to believe too easily","Her credulity made her an easy target for scams.","Skepticism"],["Morally instructive","The didactic novel aimed to teach its readers about kindness and empathy.","Uninstructive"],["To perceive or recognize","He could discern the slight differences between the original painting and the replica.","Overlook"],["Sudden realization","She had an epiphany about her career while on vacation.","Confusion"],["Having or showing great knowledge or learning","The professor’s erudite lecture on quantum physics left the students in awe of his expertise.","Ignorant, Uneducated"]],[["Understood only by a few","The philosopher's writings were so esoteric that only a small group of scholars could fully understand them.","Common"],["Very careful, attentive to detail","Her fastidious attention to detail made her an excellent editor.","Careless"],["Tact, elegant skill","She handled the negotiations with great finesse.","Clumsiness"],["To confuse","The complex instructions flummoxed everyone trying to assemble the furniture.","Clarify"],["Foolishness","It was pure folly to climb the mountain during a snowstorm.","Wisdom"],["Recklessly daring","His foolhardy decision to swim in the dangerous waters nearly cost him his life.","Cautious"],["Pompous, pretentious","His grandiose plans for the party were far beyond their budget.","Modest"],["Senseless, stupid","The comedian's jokes were so inane that few people laughed.","Insightful"],["Incompetence","His ineptitude at handling customer complaints cost the company several clients.","Skill"],["Unsophisticated, naive","Her ingenuous nature made her an easy target for scams.","Skeptical"],["Graceful, supple","The dancer’s lithe movements captivated the audience.","Stiff"],["Beginner","As a neophyte in the field, she had a lot to learn from her more experienced colleagues.","Expert"],["Mistake","The oversight in the report was quickly corrected before the meeting.","Accuracy"],["Careful, diligent","The researcher conducted a painstaking analysis of the data.","Careless"],["Overly focused on rules or details","His pedantic approach to teaching bored many of his students.","Casual"],["Showing early development in maturity or intelligence","The precocious child could read by the age of three.","Slow"],["Narrow-minded, unsophisticated","His provincial views on art made him dismissive of modern styles.","Cosmopolitan"],["Meticulous, attentive to detail","He was punctilious in keeping his financial records in perfect order.","Careless"],["A knowledgeable commentator","The political pundit offered insightful commentary during the debate.","Amateur"],["Foolish, unrealistic","His quixotic plan to start a business with no experience was bound to fail.","Practical"],["Wise","The sage advice from her mentor guided her through many difficult decisions.","Foolish"],["Very careful, precise","Her scrupulous attention to detail ensured that no mistakes were made in the report.","Careless"],["Astute, smart","The shrewd investor made profitable decisions even in a volatile market.","Naive"],["Careless, sloppy","His slipshod work on the project caused many issues later on.","Meticulous"],["To stun or shock someone","The sudden announcement of his promotion stupefied him, leaving him speechless.","Enlighten, Awaken"]],[["Easily influenced or affected","Children are often more susceptible to illnesses during the winter.","Resistant"],["Easily managed or controlled","The dog's tractable nature made him easy to train.","Stubborn"],["Extraordinary, weird","He had an uncanny ability to predict the outcome of the games.","Normal"],["Crude, lacking manners","His uncouth behavior at the dinner shocked everyone.","Polished"],["Incomprehensible, unbelievable","The vastness of space is unfathomable to the human mind.","Understandable"],["Clumsy, awkward","The ungainly teenager tripped over his own feet.","Graceful"],["Elegant, sophisticated","His urbane manners made him a favorite at social gatherings.","Unrefined"],["Commanding respect because of age or dignity","The venerable professor was admired by students and colleagues alike.","Disreputable"],["One with exceptional musical skill","The young violinist was a virtuoso, performing with a depth beyond his years.","Amateur"],["Clever or grim sense of humor","His wry comments often lightened the mood during tense moments.","Serious"],["To strengthen or support with additional evidence","The witness’s testimony corroborated the alibi.","Contradict"],["Order, politeness","Her sense of decorum was evident in how she handled the situation.","Rudeness"],["Fair, even-handed","The judge made an equitable decision based on the evidence presented.","Biased"],["Illegal","He was arrested for his involvement in illicit activities.","Legal"],["To accuse someone of a crime","The evidence incriminated him in the robbery.","Exonerate"],["Formally accuse of a crime","The grand jury indicted him on several charges of fraud.","Acquit"],["Angered by injustice","She was indignant when she learned she was passed over for promotion due to her gender.","Content"],["Lenient","His indulgent parents never disciplined him, no matter what he did.","Strict"],["Fair, showing good judgment","The committee made a judicious decision that benefited everyone.","Unwise"],["To approve or confirm","The treaty was ratified by both countries.","Reject"],["To formally approve","The board sanctioned the new policy with a unanimous vote.","Disapprove"],["To clear of blame or suspicion","The new evidence vindicated the man, proving he was innocent of the crime.","Blame"],["Generous, selfless","Her altruistic nature drove her to volunteer at the shelter every weekend.","Selfish"],["Greed","His avarice led him to make unethical business decisions.","Generosity"],["Well-meaning and kindly; showing goodwill","The benevolent stranger offered to help the lost tourists find their way.","Malevolent, Unkind"]],[["To hand down through a will","He bequeathed his estate to his children in his will.","Disinherit"],["Decrease in value","The depreciation of the car's value was expected after five years of use.","Appreciation"],["Poor, lacking necessities","The charity aims to help destitute families get back on their feet.","Affluent"],["Too expensive","The prices in the city were exorbitant compared to those in the countryside.","Reasonable"],["Cheap, economical","His frugal habits allowed him to save money over the years.","Extravagant"],["Profitable","She left her job to pursue a more lucrative career in finance.","Unprofitable"],["Lush, elaborate","The garden was filled with luxuriant plants and flowers.","Sparse"],["Generous","His magnanimous donation helped build a new school in the village.","Selfish"],["Motivated by money","The mercenary soldier fought for whoever paid him the most.","Altruistic"],["Cheap, stingy","His miserly habits made him wealthy but also left him friendless.","Generous"],["To financially support or to condescend","She patronizes the local coffee shop every morning.","Boycott"],["Stingy, poor","His penurious lifestyle was evident in his refusal to spend money on anything unnecessary.","Generous"],["An additional payment or bonus","One of the perquisites of his job was access to the company car.","Disadvantage"],["Someone who supports charity","The philanthropist donated millions to help fund education programs.","Miser"],["To get or provide","She procured the necessary documents for her application.","Lose"],["Prudent, frugal","His provident savings ensured he had a comfortable retirement.","Wasteful"],["To waste","He squandered his inheritance on frivolous purchases.","Save"],["Willing to accept bribes","The venal politician was caught accepting money in exchange for favors.","Honest"],["Career","She felt that teaching was her true vocation.","Hobby"],["Deviation from the norm","The storm was an aberration, as the region usually experiences mild weather.","Normalcy"],["To confront","He was accosted by a stranger demanding money.","Avoid"],["Not yielding","She was adamant in her decision and refused to change her mind.","Flexible"],["Lacking interest","The student's apathetic attitude towards the class was concerning.","Interested"],["Influence, domination","His ascendancy in the company was undeniable after his promotion to CEO.","Subordination"],["Characterized by severe self-discipline and abstention from indulgence, often for religious reasons","The monk led an ascetic lifestyle, choosing to live in solitude and refrain from material possessions.","Indulgent, Extravagant"]],[["Dignified","The august presence of the queen commanded respect.","Undignified"],["Dictator, dictatorial","The autocrat ruled the country with an iron fist.","Democrat"],["A person who acts like a robot","He worked like an automaton, without showing any emotion.","Individual"],["Common, lacking originality","The movie was filled with banal dialogues and predictable plots.","Original"],["Supported by two opposing groups (political parties)","The law was passed with surprising bipartisanship.","Partisanship"],["To remove from power","The dictator was deposed by a peaceful revolution.","Instate"],["Not original","His style is derivative, clearly influenced by older artists.","Innovative"],["Violation of something sacred","The desecration of the historic site caused public outrage.","Sanctification"],["Dictator","The despot imposed strict laws and suppressed freedom.","Libertarian"],["Religious, political, or philosophical principles","The political party adhered strictly to its doctrine.","Heresy"],["Forcing one's own opinions on others","He was so dogmatic that he refused to listen to anyone else’s ideas.","Open-minded"],["From diverse sources","Her taste in music is eclectic, ranging from classical to jazz.","Narrow"],["Belief in equality","She is an egalitarian who supports equal rights for all.","Elitist"],["Deliberately attracting attention","His exhibitionistic behavior was meant to impress his peers.","Reserved"],["A group within a larger group","A faction within the party opposed the new policy.","Unity"],["Excessive enthusiasm","His fanaticism for the team made him attend every game, regardless of the weather.","Indifference"],["Common, overused","The novel’s hackneyed plot made it uninteresting.","Fresh"],["Belief contrary to the established opinion","His ideas were considered heresy by the conservative members of the church.","Orthodoxy"],["Unique personal trait","His habit of wearing mismatched socks was just one of his idiosyncrasies.","Conformity"],["Conservative, traditional","The family followed orthodox customs passed down for generations.","Unorthodox"],["One who completely opposes violence","As a pacifist, he refused to join the army.","Warmonger"],["Biased supporter","He is a partisan of the ruling party, rarely critical of its decisions.","Neutral"],["Religious devotion","Her piety led her to spend hours in prayer each day.","Irreverence"],["Controversial","His polemical writing style often sparked heated debates.","Non-controver sial"],["To formally declare one's abandonment of a claim, right, or possession","After much contemplation, he decided to renounce his membership in the club.","Embrace, Retain"]],[["Respectful, showing deep respect","The crowd was reverent as the hero’s achievements were recounted.","Disrespectful"],["Holiness, sacredness","The sanctity of the ancient temple was respected by all visitors.","Profanity"],["Loyal and committed","He was a staunch supporter of animal rights.","Disloyal"],["Standard, common","His speech was filled with stock phrases, lacking originality.","Unique"],["Loud and harsh","The strident alarm woke everyone in the building.","Soft"],["Seeking to overthrow","The book was banned for its subversive ideas.","Loyal"],["To replace","Newer technologies have supplanted older devices.","Retain"],["Flatterer, someone who acts obsequiously","He was known as a sycophant, always agreeing with the boss.","Critic"],["A person who behaves obsequiously","The toady eagerly complimented his manager at every opportunity.","Opponent"],["Undemocratic, authoritarian control","The totalitarian regime controlled every aspect of citizens' lives.","Democratic"],["Common, overused","His essay was filled with trite expressions.","Original"],["To seize power unlawfully","The general attempted to usurp the throne.","Relinquish"],["Fanatic, excessively enthusiastic","He was a zealot, willing to sacrifice everything for his beliefs.","Moderate"],["To attack verbally","The politician was assailed by critics.","Defend"],["To scold harshly","The coach berated the team for their poor performance.","Praise"],["To punish or criticize severely","The teacher castigated the student for cheating.","Commend"],["Harshly critical","Her censorious remarks offended her friends.","Approving"],["To scold or reprimand","The official was censured for his misconduct.","Applaud"],["To punish or criticize","The mother chastised her son for his misbehavior.","Praise"],["To scold","She chided her friend for being late.","Compliment"],["Dismay, worry","He looked at the broken vase with consternation.","Relief"],["Showing disdain","Her contemptuous remarks upset her colleagues.","Respectful"],["Despicable, deserving of disdain","The contemptible behavior shocked the community.","Honorable"],["Deserving blame or censure; guilty","The manager was culpable for the violations.","Innocent, Blameless"],["Criticize unfairly","She was denignated by scholars.","Praise"]],[["To express disapproval of","He deprecated the idea of increasing taxes.","Approve"],["To mock or ridicule","The critics derided the actor's latest performance.","Praise"],["Showing a critical or disrespectful attitude","The derogatory comments hurt her feelings.","Complimentar y"],["To disregard or dismiss as unimportant","He discounted her concerns about the project.","Consider"],["To belittle or speak down on","She disparaged his achievements in front of others.","Compliment"],["A speech or piece of writing praising someone","The eulogy highlighted all of his major life accomplishments.","Criticism"],["To praise enthusiastically","The teacher extolled the student's dedication to her studies.","Condemn"],["To give praise; praiseworthy","The company received laudatory reviews for its innovation.","Disparaging"],["Harmful, poisonous","The noxious fumes from the factory posed a health hazard.","Harmless"],["Deserving condemnation","His reprehensible actions led to his expulsion from school.","Admirable"],["A formal expression of disapproval","The employee received a reprimand for his tardiness.","Commendatio n"],["To express disappointment or disapproval","She reproached him for being late to the meeting.","Praise"],["Severely critical","The scathing review damaged the author's reputation.","Mild"],["To insult by treating with neglect","She felt slighted when they didn’t invite her to the party.","Compliment"],["To reject with disdain or contempt","He spurned her offer to help with the project.","Accept"],["A long, angry speech","His tirade about the unfair treatment lasted over an hour.","Compliment"],["To publicly praise or promote","The company touted its new product as a game-changer.","Criticize"],["Pretentious, designed to impress","His affected accent made him sound insincere.","Genuine"],["Distress or embarrassment at having failed","Much to his chagrin, he was not chosen for the promotion.","Satisfaction"],["A self-satisfied attitude with no desire to improve","His complacency led to a decline in the company’s performance.","Ambition"],["To soothe anger, make peace","He made a conciliatory gesture by apologizing first.","Antagonize"],["The act of lowering in dignity or status","The degradation of the environment is a global concern.","Improvement"],["Modest and reserved in behavior","Her demure appearance belied her inner strength.","Bold"],["Lacking proper respect or seriousness","His flippant remarks about the serious issue upset everyone.","Serious"],["Excessive pride or self-confidence, often leading to downfall","His hubris blinded him to the potential risks, ultimately leading to the failure of his project.","Humility, Modesty"]],[["Public shame or disgrace","His ignominious defeat ended his career in politics.","Honor"],["Assuming power or authority without justification","His imperious tone alienated his colleagues.","Submissive"],["Not showing respect for others","The child was punished for his impudence toward the teacher.","Politeness"],["Rude and disrespectful behavior","Her insolent reply shocked everyone in the room.","Respectful"],["Lack of respect for serious things","His irreverent comments during the meeting were inappropriate.","Respectful"],["Famous for something bad","The notorious gangster was finally arrested.","Obscurity"],["Stubbornly refusing to change one's opinion","Despite the evidence, he remained obdurate in his stance.","Compliant"],["Stubbornly refusing to change despite attempts to persuade","His obstinate refusal to cooperate caused delays.","Agreeable"],["Taking advantage of opportunities with little regard for principle","The opportunistic politician changed his views to gain more support.","Principled"],["Insisting on immediate attention or obedience","The officer gave a peremptory command to the soldiers.","Hesitant"],["Overstepping bounds, inappropriate boldness","It was presumptuous of him to assume she would agree.","Humble"],["Having an uncooperative attitude towards authority","The recalcitrant student refused to follow the teacher's instructions.","Compliant"],["Believing one's own actions and opinions are morally superior","Her self-righteous attitude alienated her friends.","Modest"],["Prioritizing one's own advantage over others","His self-serving behavior damaged his relationships with colleagues.","Altruistic"],["Behaving as if superior to others","The supercilious waiter made the guests feel unwelcome.","Humble"],["Not embarrassed or ashamed","She was unabashed in her pursuit of success.","Ashamed"],["Difficult to control or predict","His wayward behavior made him difficult to manage.","Docile"],["To be hindered or stalled","He got bogged down in the details of the project.","Advance"],["To come together to form one whole","The different factions coalesced into a united group.","Separate"],["The junction of two rivers, or the merging of ideas","There was a confluence of new ideas at the conference.","Divergence"],["To spread widely","The internet allows information to be disseminated rapidly.","Conceal"],["To bubble, fizz, or show enthusiasm","Her effervescent personality made her the life of the party.","Flat"],["To draw out a response or reaction","His question elicited a thoughtful answer.","Suppress"],["Originating in a particular place","The indigenous people of the region have lived there for centuries.","Foreign"],["To cause","Their fight induced their expulsion form the school.","effect"]],[["Not moving or active","The rock remained inert for centuries.","Active"],["Intrinsic, natural","She has an inherent talent for music.","Acquired"],["Having many types","The multifarious talents of the artist amazed everyone.","Limited"],["Outcome","The heavy rain precipitated a flood.","Delay"],["To lessen","The storm finally abated after hours of chaos.","Intensify"],["To assign or portion","They allocated a section of the budget for research.","Withhold"],["Waste away","The patient's muscles began to atrophy from lack of use.","Strengthen"],["To weaken or reduce","The signal was attenuated as it passed through the walls.","Strengthen"],["To grow or flourish","Her interest in science burgeoned after the field trip.","Decline"],["To restrict","Their activities were circumscribed by the new regulations.","Expand"],["Abundant","She took copious notes during the lecture.","Scarce"],["Scarcity","There was a dearth of volunteers for the project.","Abundance"],["Lacking","The desert is devoid of water.","Full"],["To spread out","The light diffused through the frosted glass.","Concentrate"],["Extremely small","The diminutive bird fit easily in the palm of his hand.","Large"],["To erase","Time had effaced the memories of his childhood.","Preserve"],["To include or surround","The syllabus encompasses all areas of the subject.","Exclude"],["Intrusive","The weeds were encroaching on the garden.","Receding"],["To unearth or dig up","Archaeologists excavated the ancient city.","Bury"],["To disentangle","She extricated herself from the awkward situation.","Entangle"],["Gigantic","The gargantuan statue towered over the park.","Tiny"],["(Cause to) grow","The seeds began to germinate after being planted.","Wither"],["To hinder or restrict","The heavy traffic hampered their journey.","Aid"],["To develop or grow","The eggs were incubated under controlled conditions.","Halt"],["Done at random or without careful judgment; not selective","The indiscriminate use of pesticides harmed not only pests but also beneficial insects in the garden.","Discriminate, Selective"]],[["To restrain or hinder","Fear of failure can inhibit success.","Encourage"],["Inborn or natural","She has an innate ability to communicate.","Acquired"],["Harmless","His joke was innocuous, but it still offended some people.","Harmful"],["Isolated or narrow-minded","His insular views made it difficult to discuss global issues.","Open-minded"],["To overwhelm or flood","The city was inundated by a massive storm.","Drain"],["Present but not visible or active","The latent talent of the student was revealed in the final exam.","Active"],["To make less severe or serious","They tried to mitigate the damage caused by the hurricane.","Aggravate"],["A small quantity","He showed a modicum of respect during the debate.","Abundance"],["Varied or diverse","The motley crew included people from all walks of life.","Homogeneou s"],["To dry out or dehydrate","The sun parched the land, leaving it barren.","Moisten"],["A scarcity or lack of something","There is a paucity of evidence to support the claim.","Abundance"],["On the edge or outer boundary","The issue was peripheral to the main discussion.","Central"],["The ability to be shaped or molded","The plasticity of the brain allows it to adapt to new experiences.","Rigidity"],["An excessive amount","The plethora of options made it hard to choose a restaurant.","Scarcity"],["Easily bent or influenced","The pliable clay was perfect for sculpting.","Rigid"],["To prevent or make impossible","His injury precluded him from playing in the game.","Allow"],["Remarkably large or impressive","He had a prodigious appetite, eating five plates of food.","Small"],["Plentiful or abundant","The profusion of flowers made the garden beautiful.","Sparse"],["Excessively high or restrictive","The cost of the car was prohibitive for most buyers.","Affordable"],["To increase rapidly","The company has proliferated since launching its new product.","Diminish"],["Productive or creative","She is a prolific writer, publishing several books a year.","Unproductive"],["To suppress or put an end to","The police were called to quell the riot.","Encourage"],["Spreading unchecked","Crime was rampant in the city during the 90s.","Controlled"],["Extremely hungry","After the hike, he was ravenous and ate everything in sight.","Full"],["To gather or harvest, especially crops","After months of hard work, they were finally able to reap the rewards of their efforts.","Sow, plant"]],[["Tending to recede or go backward","The gene for blue eyes is recessive.","Dominant"],["To assign to a lower position","She was relegated to a smaller role in the play.","Promote"],["To give up or surrender","He relinquished control of the company to his partner.","Retain"],["A collection of plays or works","The theater company had a large repertory of Shakespearean plays.","Single piece"],["To satisfy fully","The large meal satiated his hunger.","Deprive"],["To soak or fill completely","The rain saturated the soil.","Dry"],["Small or insufficient in quantity","His scanty salary was barely enough to pay rent.","Abundant"],["The range or extent of something","The scope of the project was much larger than expected.","Limitation"],["More than what is needed","She bought a superfluous amount of decorations for the party.","Necessary"],["An excessive amount","The surfeit of food at the banquet was overwhelming.","Shortage"],["To be full of or swarming with","The pond was teeming with fish.","Empty"],["Of little importance or value","Their argument was over a trifling matter.","Significant"],["Present everywhere","Smartphones have become ubiquitous in modern society.","Rare"],["Lacking thought or intelligence","His vacuous expression showed he wasn't paying attention.","Insightful"],["Thick and sticky","The viscous syrup slowly dripped from the bottle.","Fluid"],["Decreasing in size or strength","His influence over the team was waning.","Increasing"],["Complex and intricate","The byzantine nature of the tax code confuses many people.","Simple"],["Harsh or discordant sounds","The cacophonous noise from the construction site was unbearable.","Harmonious"],["Hasty and not thorough","He gave the report a cursory glance before the meeting.","Thorough"],["A person's manner of walking","His slow gait suggested he was tired.","Posture"],["Excessively bright or flashy","The garish colors of the outfit made her stand out.","Subtle"],["Someone who consumes too much food or drink","He was a glutton at the buffet, trying every dish.","Moderate"],["Vivid in a shocking way","The lurid details of the crime fascinated the media.","Dull"],["Easily influenced or shaped","The clay was malleable in her hands as she formed the sculpture.","Rigid"],["In a state of severe disrepair","The old ramshackle house looked like it could collapse at any moment.","Well-built"]],[["Strongly reminiscent or suggestive of","The air was redolent with the smell of pine trees.","Odorless"],["To cover or hide","The mountain was shrouded in mist.","Reveal"],["Complete or sheer; severe in appearance","The stark contrast between light and dark was striking.","Softness"],["Juicy or rich in desirable qualities","The succulent steak was cooked to perfection.","Dry"],["Extremely old or outdated","His ideas were antediluvian and no longer relevant.","Modern"],["Slow to act","The government was criticized for its dilatory response to the crisis.","Prompt"],["Lasting for a very short time","The ephemeral beauty of the sunset left everyone in awe.","Permanent"],["To move or act quickly","She hastened to finish the project before the deadline.","Delay"],["A person or thing regarded as an infallible authority","The oracle predicted the future with great accuracy.","Ignoramus"],["Expected or likely to happen","The prospective students visited the campus.","Retrospective"],["Moving backward or returning to a previous state","The company adopted a regressive policy that hindered progress.","Progressive"],["Occurring at irregular intervals","There were sporadic outbreaks of violence throughout the city.","Constant"],["To avoid making a decision in order to gain time","The politician tried to temporize instead of addressing the issue.","Decide"],["Lasting for only a short time","The transient nature of the job meant he moved frequently.","Permanent"],["Understood by few; mysterious or secret","The professor's arcane knowledge of ancient languages fascinated the students.","Commonplace"],["To give a false impression","Her calm expression belied the anxiety she was feeling.","Reveal"],["A person falsely claiming to have special knowledge or skill","The charlatan tricked people into buying fake medicine.","Expert"],["Roundabout, not direct","The circuitous route took longer than expected.","Direct"],["Kept secret or done secretively","The clandestine meeting was held late at night.","Open"],["To make something clearer and easier to understand","The teacher demystified the complex concept with a simple explanation.","Confuse"],["Not candid or sincere","His disingenuous apology did not seem genuine.","Honest"],["To reveal something private or secret","She refused to divulge the details of the confidential agreement.","Conceal"],["To deceive or trick","He was duped into buying a fake watch.","Enlighten"],["Deceitful, double-dealing","Her duplicitous behavior made it hard to trust her.","Honest"],["Difficult to understand","Math seemed like a enigma to her, though she was good at other subjects.","Easy"]],[["A public report about wrongdoing","The exposé revealed corruption within the company.","Cover-up"],["Based on a mistaken belief","The argument was fallacious and misleading.","Logical"],["A false or mistaken idea","The belief that vaccines cause autism is a fallacy.","Truth"],["Dishonest or deceptive","The fraudulent scheme cost investors millions.","Honest"],["Attempting to avoid notice or attention","She gave him a furtive glance as she passed.","Open"],["Unwilling to believe something","She was incredulous when she heard the shocking news.","Trusting"],["Not exactly known, established, or defined","The cause of the accident is still indeterminate.","Certain"],["Impossible to understand or interpret","His inscrutable expression made it hard to tell what he was thinking.","Transparent"],["The use of words to convey a meaning that is opposite of its literal meaning","It was ironic that the fire station burned down.","Sincerity"],["Appearing to be true, but not necessarily so","The ostensible reason for his absence was illness.","Real"],["Seeming reasonable or probable","His explanation for the mistake seemed plausible.","Improbable"],["A reason given in justification that is not the real reason","He used the meeting as a pretext to leave work early.","Truth"],["A person who speaks falsely; a liar","The prevaricator twisted the truth to suit his own needs.","Honest person"],["To correct or make right","He tried to rectify his mistake by apologizing.","Worsen"],["The act of proving something wrong","The refutation of his argument was swift and thorough.","Confirmation"],["Making a show of being morally superior","His sanctimonious attitude alienated his friends.","Humble"],["The use of clever but false arguments","The politician used sophistry to win the debate.","Honesty"],["Not being what it purports to be; false or fake","The spurious documents were quickly exposed as forgeries.","Genuine"],["To provide evidence to support or prove","He could not substantiate his claims with any real evidence.","Disprove"],["Conducive to success; favorable","The sunny weather was an auspicious sign for the wedding.","Inauspicious"],["A concentrated outpouring, as of questions or blows","The reporter faced a barrage of questions from the press.","Trickle"],["Hostile and aggressive","The belligerent crowd became violent after the match.","Peaceful"],["In a state of decline or decay","The blighted neighborhood was once a thriving community.","Flourishing"],["To support or strengthen","The success of the project bolstered his confidence.","Weaken"],["To support","I buttressed m argument with an evidence","Weaken"]],[["To find a way around an obstacle","He circumvented the problem by using a different approach.","Confront"],["A large, destructive fire","The forest conflagration destroyed thousands of acres.","Extinguishin g"],["Causing or likely to cause disagreement","The contentious issue divided the community.","Agreeable"],["To destroy a large part of","The disease decimated the population of the village.","Build"],["Harmful or damaging","The chemicals had a deleterious effect on the environment.","Beneficial"],["Moral corruption","The depravity of his actions shocked the community.","Virtue"],["Extremely serious or urgent","They were in dire need of medical assistance.","Trivial"],["Differing from the standard or norm","Their divergent opinions led to a heated argument.","Convergent"],["Tending to cause disagreement or hostility","The politician's divisive rhetoric alienated many voters.","Unifying"],["To evade or escape from","The suspect managed to elude the police.","Confront"],["Difficult to find, catch, or achieve","Success remained elusive despite their best efforts.","Obtainable"],["To make someone feel bitter or resentful","The loss embittered him for years.","Soothe"],["A burden or impediment","The heavy bag was an encumbrance during the hike.","Aid"],["Happening by chance rather than intention","The meeting was a fortuitous coincidence.","Planned"],["Impaired the appearance of; disfigured","The scratch marred the surface of the table.","Enhanced"],["Wicked or criminal","The nefarious villain plotted to take over the world.","Honorable"],["To relieve or lessen without curing","The medicine palliated the symptoms but did not cure the illness.","Aggravate"],["Not securely held or in position; dangerously likely to fall or collapse","The ladder was placed in a precarious position.","Stable"],["To completely destroy","The old building was razed to make way for a new development.","Build"],["The occurrence of events by chance in a happy or beneficial way","Finding the rare book at the store was pure serendipity.","Misfortune"],["Showing the indifference to comfort or luxury","His spartan lifestyle involved few possessions and no luxuries.","Luxurious"],["To defeat thoroughly","The army vanquished its enemies in a decisive battle.","Surrender"],["Keeping careful watch for possible danger","The guards remained vigilant throughout the night.","Negligent"],["Having or showing a strong desire for revenge","Her vindictive actions were driven by years of resentment.","Forgiving"],["Extremely harmful or poisonous","The virulent strain of the virus spread rapidly, leading to a public health crisis.","Harmless, Benign"]]],"ap":[[["To publicly support or recommend a cause or policy","She advocates for animal rights by volunteering at shelters.","Oppose, criticize"],["To have enough resources to do or buy something","I can finally afford a new bike after saving for months","Lack, forfeit"],["Objective and unemotional; related to medical treatment","His clinical approach to problem-solving makes him an excellent scientist","Emotional, subjective"],["To make up or form something","These 10 players constitute the best soccer team in the league.","Disband, dissolve"],["Causing disagreement or debate","The new school policy became a controversial topic among parents.","Uncontroversial, agreeable"],["To communicate or make known","The teacher used stories to convey the importance of honesty.","Withhold, obscure"],["Having the opposite effect of what is intended","Skipping meals to lose weight is counterproductive and can harm your health","Effective, productive"],["A set of beliefs held by a group or organization","The school follows a doctrine of respect and inclusivity","Anarchy, disbelief"],["Dull, bleak, or depressing","The rainy weather made the whole day feel dreary.","Bright, cheerful"],["To involve or require as a necessary step","Becoming a doctor entails years of study and training","Exclude, eliminate"],["Firmly established and difficult to change","The tradition of Sunday family dinners is deeply entrenched in our household","Unstable, temporary"],["To change or vary irregularly","The temperature fluctuates dramatically in the desert","Stabilize, remain constant"],["To instigate or stir up","The leader’s speech was intended to foment rebellion against the unjust law","Deter, suppress"],["Relating to old age or elderly people","The hospital opened a new geriatric ward to care for older patients.","Youthful, adolescent"],["Deserving pity or sympathy","The stray dog’s pitiable condition moved everyone to tears.","Admirable, enviable"],["Dealing with things sensibly and realistically","His pragmatic approach to saving money helped him buy a car quickly.","Impractical, idealistic"],["To cause or bring about an action; immediate or on time","Her question prompted a lively discussion in the class","Discourage, delay"],["To officially charge someone with a crime and pursue legal action","The state decided to prosecute the case despite limited evidence.","Defend, pardon"],["In an unwilling or hesitant manner","He reluctantly agreed to help clean up the mess after the party.","Willingly, eagerly"],["To formally give up or reject something","He decided to renounce his claim to the inheritance for the sake of family peace","Embrace, accept"],["To refuse to accept or be associated with","The politician was quick to repudiate the allegations of corruption.","Accept, endorse"],["A view or opinion that is influenced by emotion","The heartfelt sentiment in her letter brought tears to my eyes.","Indifference, apathy"],["Of considerable importance, size, or worth","The fundraiser collected a substantial amount of money for the charity.","Insignificant, small"],["To confirm or prove something as true","The scientist’s findings were validated by further experiments.","Invalidate, disprove"],["To produce or provide; to","The farm yields enough","Resist, retain"]],[["Extremely bad or appalling","The team's performance was abysmal, leading to their early exit from the competition.","Excellent, impressive"],["To adjust or modify to suit a new environment or condition","Animals adapt to their surroundings to survive.","Resist, oppose"],["The arrival or beginning of something significant","The advent of the internet changed the way we communicate.","Departure, disappearance"],["Having a strong desire to achieve something","She is ambitious and aims to become the CEO of her company.","Unmotivated, content"],["Mixed feelings or uncertainty about something","His ambivalence about moving to a new city was clear.","Certainty, decisiveness"],["To take advantage of or profit from something","He capitalized on his unique skills to succeed in business.","Waste, overlook"],["To take into one’s possession or control by force","The photographer captured the beauty of the sunset perfectly.","Release, miss"],["To happen at the same time or to agree","The concert coincided with my birthday, making it a special day.","Differ, clash"],["To accept or allow behavior that is morally wrong","The teacher refused to condone cheating in the exam.","Condemn, punish"],["A firmly held belief or the act of declaring someone guilty","Her conviction in her ideals inspired others to follow her.","Doubt, acquittal"],["To raise objections or show reluctance","She agreed without demur to the proposal.","Accept, agree"],["To encourage or stir up violent or unlawful behavior","The speech was accused of inciting violence among the crowd.","Calm, pacify"],["A reversal of position, order, or relationship","The inversion of roles in the play made it interesting.","Consistency, continuity"],["Not overly proud or boastful; small or moderate","He remained modest despite his great achievements.","Arrogant, boastful"],["Having unlimited power; able to do anything","The ruler considered himself omnipotent and ruled with an iron fist.","Powerless, weak"],["To express an opinion","He opined that the new policy would benefit small businesses.","Silence, withhold"],["To remove from a position or place","The board decided to oust the CEO due to poor performance.","Install, retain"],["To spread or branch out into smaller divisions","The decision could ramify into unexpected consequences.","Simplify, consolidate"],["Uncooked or in a natural state","He prefers eating raw vegetables for a healthy diet.","Cooked, refined"],["The ability to keep or hold something","The company focuses on employee retention to maintain its workforce.","Loss, turnover"],["Lacking movement or change","The market remained static despite the new policy announcements.","Dynamic, active"],["Lower in rank or position","As a subordinate officer, she followed orders without question.","Superior, chief"],["Not certain or fixed; provisional","The meeting date is tentative and subject to change.","Definite, certain"],["A prejudice for or against something","The article showed a clear bias towards one political party.","Impartiality, fairness"],["Able to be compared; similar","The two houses are comparable in price and size.","Different, dissimilar"]],[["To admit or acknowledge something as true","She conceded her mistake after reviewing the evidence.","Deny, reject"],["To organize or carry out a task","The scientist conducted an experiment to test the hypothesis.","Neglect, mismanage"],["To nurture or improve something, often by effort","He cultivated a love for reading in his children.","Ignore, neglect"],["An official order issued by an authority","The king issued a decree banning the practice.","Suggestion, request"],["Extremely serious or urgent","The refugees were in dire need of food and water.","Trivial, minor"],["Disagreement or conflict between people","The meeting ended in discord, with no resolution reached.","Harmony, agreement"],["To belittle or speak down to someone","He disparaged her efforts despite her hard work.","Praise, commend"],["A feeling of jealousy towards someone's possessions or achievements","Her new car was the envy of the neighborhood.","Contentment, goodwill"],["To use something or someone unfairly for personal gain","The company exploited its workers by underpaying them.","Respect, conserve"],["Existing as an idea but not having a physical form","Her painting depicted abstract concepts like freedom and love.","Concrete, tangible"],["Concerned with beauty or the appreciation of beauty","The garden was designed with great aesthetic appeal.","Unattractive, unaesthetic"],["To disturb or upset someone","The loud noise agitated the sleeping baby.","Calm, soothe"],["To indirectly refer to something","The author alluded to historical events in the novel.","Specify, declare"],["A noisy argument or disagreement","The altercation between the neighbors woke everyone up.","Agreement, peace"],["The quality of being genuine or real","The museum verified the authenticity of the ancient artifact.","Falseness, imitation"],["To make an action or process easier","The new software will facilitate faster data analysis.","Hinder, obstruct"],["Relating to government revenue, especially taxes","The fiscal policy aims to reduce the national debt.","Nonfinancial, irrelevant"],["Able to be predicted or anticipated","No major changes are expected in the foreseeable future.","Unpredictable, uncertain"],["Acting without concern for rules or consequences","The freewheeling lifestyle of the artist shocked his family.","Restrained, cautious"],["Impressive or grand in appearance","The imposing building towered over the skyline.","Unimpressive, modest"],["The act of forcing something on someone","The imposition of new taxes angered the citizens.","Relief, removal"],["The ability to move from one place to another","The invention of the wheel revolutionized human locomotion.","Immobility, stillness"],["To formally forbid something by law or rule","Smoking is prohibited in public buildings.","Allow, permit"],["To officially announce or make widely known","The government promulgated new safety regulations.","Conceal, suppress"],["The act of thinking again about a decision","After much reconsideration, she decided to take the job offer.","Decision, resolution"]],[["To make changes in something to improve it","The government promised to reform the education system.","Maintain, worsen"],["Very careful and thorough","She was scrupulous in checking her calculations.","Careless, negligent"],["Unity or agreement among individuals with a common interest","The workers showed solidarity during the strike.","Disunity, discord"],["To produce or generate something","The success of the movie spawned several sequels.","Destroy, suppress"],["Delicate or precise, not obvious","The artist used subtle shades to create depth in the painting.","Obvious, blunt"],["Enough to meet the needs of something","He had sufficient funds to buy the car.","Insufficient, inadequate"],["To release or give off","The factory emits a lot of smoke into the air.","Absorb, contain"],["Expressing something forcibly and clearly","She was emphatic about her decision to leave.","Hesitant, uncertain"],["To mention things one by one","He enumerated the reasons for his decision.","Generalize, overlook"],["Likely to be influenced or harmed by something","Young children are more susceptible to colds.","Resistant, immune"],["Involving conflict or opposition","The debate took on an adversarial tone.","Friendly, cooperative"],["Strict or severe in manner","The monk lived an austere life in the mountains.","Luxurious, indulgent"],["Both pleasant and painful at the same time","Graduation day was a bittersweet moment for everyone.","Unmixed, unalloyed"],["The quality of being open and honest","She spoke with candor about her experiences.","Deception, insincerity"],["To take or hold something by force","The photograph perfectly captured the moment.","Release, miss"],["Something that completes or goes well with something else","The wine was a perfect complement to the meal.","Clash, contrast"],["Making a certain situation likely or possible","The quiet environment was conducive to studying.","Hindering, unfavorable"],["To tell someone a secret in trust","He confided his fears to his closest friend.","Conceal, suppress"],["To say the opposite of something","His actions contradict his words.","Confirm, agree"],["A situation requiring a choice between equally undesirable options","She faced a dilemma about whether to move abroad or stay.","Certainty, resolution"],["Outstandingly bad or shocking","The company made an egregious error in their calculations.","Minor, slight"],["Not regular or consistent","Her attendance at work has been erratic lately.","Steady, consistent"],["To set up or found something","The school was established in 1905.","Destroy, dismantle"],["To express sorrow or regret","She lamented the loss of her childhood home.","Celebrate, rejoice"],["Exaggeratedly emotional or sentimental","The actor's performance was overly melodramatic.","Subtle, restrained"]],[["The quality of being unbiased and impartial","The judge's objectivity was praised during the trial.","Bias, subjectivity"],["To die or be destroyed","Many ancient manuscripts perished in the fire.","Survive, endure"],["An earlier event or action regarded as an example","This case sets a precedent for future decisions.","Novelty, innovation"],["A person who held a job before someone else","The new CEO thanked her predecessor for his contributions.","Successor, follower"],["A fundamental truth or proposition serving as a foundation","She lived by the principle of honesty.","Disregard, chaos"],["To encourage or stimulate action","The discovery spurred further research.","Discourage, hinder"],["Stretched or pulled tight","The rope was taut and ready to use.","Loose, slack"],["Plain and without decoration","The room was unadorned but clean.","Ornate, decorated"],["To reveal or disclose","The company unveiled its latest product at the conference.","Conceal, hide"],["To plan or invent something","They devised a strategy to win the game.","Destroy, disorganize"],["To send off to a destination for a purpose","The goods were dispatched promptly to the customer.","Recall, retain"],["Control or the exercise of control","The king held dominion over the entire region.","Subservience, submission"],["To suffer patiently or to last over time","She endured the long journey with grace.","Give up, surrender"],["To bring or recall to the mind","The painting evoked memories of her childhood.","Suppress, ignore"],["To make a situation worse","His comments only exacerbated the tension in the room.","Alleviate, reduce"],["Shocking or exciting to action","The speech was galvanizing and motivated the crowd to act.","Demotivating, discouraging"],["To communicate or bestow information","The teacher imparted valuable knowledge to the students.","Withhold, suppress"],["Not showing care for the consequences of an action","His imprudent decision led to financial losses.","Prudent, careful"],["Lack of interest or concern","Her indifference to the problem frustrated her team.","Concern, interest"],["The act of gaining or obtaining something","The company's acquisition of new technology boosted profits.","Loss, forfeiture"],["To destroy completely","The army annihilated the enemy forces.","Preserve, save"],["Something that deviates from what is normal","The scientist found an anomaly in the data.","Normality, regularity"],["Made by humans, not natural","The flowers were artificial but looked real.","Natural, genuine"],["A path or approach to achieving something","Education is an important avenue to success.","Blockage, barrier"],["General agreement","The committee reached a consensus on the budget plan.","Disagreement, conflict"]],[["To show or explain something clearly","The scientist demonstrated how the experiment works.","Conceal, obscure"],["To allow oneself to enjoy the pleasure of something","She indulged in her favorite chocolate dessert.","Deprive, restrain"],["Featuring new methods; advanced and original","The company is known for its innovative technology.","Conventional, unoriginal"],["To call upon something, especially a law or principle","The lawyer invoked a new precedent in the case.","Dismiss, waive"],["Childishly sulky or bad-tempered","His petulant behavior irritated everyone at the meeting.","Patient, agreeable"],["Acting without careful consideration","His rash decision led to financial problems.","Cautious, prudent"],["Without hesitation; willingly","She readily agreed to help with the project.","Reluctantly, unwillingly"],["Causing general public outrage","The politician was involved in a scandalous affair.","Respectable, honorable"],["The feeling of contempt or disdain","He looked at her with scorn after the argument.","Respect, admiration"],["After a particular thing has happened","He moved to New York and subsequently found a job.","Previously, beforehand"],["Present or existing everywhere","Smartphones have become ubiquitous in modern life.","Rare, uncommon"],["Performed by or affecting only one side","The decision was made unilaterally by the manager.","Bilateral, mutual"],["To strongly recommend or encourage","She urged her friends to join the charity event.","Dissuade, discourage"],["To struggle to surmount a difficulty","He contended with financial problems for years.","Yield, concede"],["Deserted and bleak","The desolate landscape stretched for miles.","Populated, thriving"],["To make or become less","Her influence in the company diminished over time.","Increase, amplify"],["Without careful distinction or choice","The bombings were carried out indiscriminately.","Selectively, carefully"],["Of great importance or significance","The signing of the treaty was a momentous occasion.","Trivial, insignificant"],["Having great power or influence","The medicine was so potent that it worked immediately.","Weak, ineffective"],["To prove to be false or incorrect","She refuted the claims made by the opposition.","Confirm, validate"],["To strengthen or support","The soldiers reinforced their position on the battlefield.","Weaken, undermine"],["To express disapproval or disappointment","He reproached his son for skipping school.","Praise, commend"],["To examine closely and thoroughly","The auditor scrutinized the company's financial records.","Overlook, ignore"],["Bad-tempered and unfriendly","The waiter was surly and rude to the customers.","Friendly, pleasant"],["To overcome a difficulty or obstacle","She surmounted numerous challenges to achieve her dream.","Fail, surrender"]],[["Showing sensitivity in dealing with others","She gave a tactful response to the sensitive question.","Insensitive, thoughtless"],["A person's or animal's nature","Her cheerful temperament made her popular among friends.","Moodiness, irritability"],["Guilty of or involving betrayal; dangerous","The journey through the mountains was treacherous.","Loyal, safe"],["To move with a smooth, wave-like motion","The flag undulated in the breeze.","Still, flat"],["To be exceptionally good at something","He excels in mathematics and science.","Fail, underperform"],["Skilled or proficient at something","She is adept at solving complex problems.","Incompetent, unskilled"],["To give permission for something","The teacher allowed students to leave early.","Forbid, deny"],["To expect or predict","We anticipate a large crowd at the event.","Doubt, disregard"],["To support or strengthen","The team bolstered their defense with a new player.","Weaken, undermine"],["Honest and straightforward","She gave a candid opinion about the project.","Deceptive, reserved"],["Rough or crude in texture or manner","The coarse fabric irritated her skin.","Smooth, refined"],["Having the necessary ability or skills","She is highly competent in her field.","Incompetent, inept"],["The highest point of something","Winning the championship was the culmination of their efforts.","Beginning, nadir"],["Lacking in some necessary quality or element","Her diet was deficient in essential vitamins.","Sufficient, adequate"],["Feeling distressed or shocked","He was dismayed by the sudden change in plans.","Comforted, reassured"],["Hesitating or doubting","She was dubious about the plan's success.","Certain, confident"],["Famous and respected in a field","He is an eminent scientist known for his research.","Obscure, unknown"],["To apply effort or influence","She exerted all her strength to lift the box.","Relax, refrain"],["Making one feel very happy or thrilled","The roller coaster ride was exhilarating.","Dull, boring"],["Unfriendly or antagonistic","The atmosphere in the room was hostile after the argument.","Friendly, amicable"],["Based on a possible idea or situation","The professor presented a hypothetical scenario to explain the concept.","Actual, real"],["To deduce or conclude from evidence","From his silence, I inferred he was upset.","Misunderstand, confuse"],["To make changes to something","The rules were modified to accommodate new players.","Preserve, maintain"],["Having no legal or binding force","The contract was declared null and void.","Valid, binding"],["The beginning or start of something","The onset of winter brought heavy snow.","End, conclusion"]],[["Elaborately decorated","The ornate palace impressed the visitors.","Plain, simple"],["Causing anger or strong reaction","The provocative article sparked a heated debate.","Uninspiring, dull"],["Relating to measurable quantities","The report focused on quantitative data analysis.","Qualitative, descriptive"],["Complete and utter","The sheer size of the mountain was awe-inspiring.","Partial, limited"],["Easily understood or done","The instructions were simple to follow.","Complex, complicated"],["Giving the impression of harm","The abandoned house had a sinister appearance.","Innocent, harmless"],["Extremely dirty and unpleasant","They lived in squalid conditions.","Clean, tidy"],["Easy to perceive or detect","The glass was so transparent that it was nearly invisible.","Opaque, unclear"],["Very great in amount or intensity","The team made tremendous progress in a short time.","Small, insignificant"],["Not based on fairness","The ruling was deemed unjust by many.","Fair, just"],["In a way that is appropriate","She adjusted her plans accordingly.","Inappropriately, unsuitably"],["A strong feeling of dislike","He felt an antipathy toward dishonesty.","Affinity, liking"],["Anxiety or fear about something","Her apprehension about the test was evident.","Confidence, assurance"],["Having an eager desire for something","He is an avid reader of mystery novels.","Apathetic, indifferent"],["Fundamental or essential","Learning the basic concepts is important.","Complex, advanced"],["To increase or improve something","The new ad campaign boosted sales significantly.","Reduce, decrease"],["An instruction or command","The artist received a commission to paint a portrait.","Dismissal, refusal"],["To keep within limits","The patient was confined to his room.","Free, release"],["To neutralize the effects of something","The antidote counteracted the poison.","Promote, enhance"],["An argument made to oppose another argument","The lawyer presented a strong counterargument.","Agreement, support"],["Based on observation or experience","The study provided empirical evidence for the theory.","Theoretical, speculative"],["To use up resources","The project expended a lot of time and money.","Save, conserve"],["In an honest and direct way","She spoke frankly about her mistakes.","Deceptively, dishonestly"],["Producing a great deal of profit","The business turned out to be highly lucrative.","Unprofitable, worthless"],["Easily influenced or shaped","Gold is a malleable metal.","Rigid, inflexible"]],[["Overly concerned with material possessions","He was criticized for his materialistic values.","Spiritual, nonmaterialistic"],["New or original","The scientist proposed a novel approach to the problem.","Old, traditional"],["No longer in use","Typewriters have become obsolete.","Modern, current"],["Strange or unusual","She had a peculiar habit of humming while working.","Normal, ordinary"],["To harass or oppress","They were persecuted for their beliefs.","Protect, support"],["A peculiar behavioral trait","His quirk of tapping his fingers was noticeable.","Normality, commonality"],["Satisfied to the full","The delicious meal left him completely satiated.","Hungry, unsatisfied"],["Practical knowledge and ability","She is very savvy about social media trends.","Clueless, inexperienced"],["To produce and release a substance","The glands secrete hormones into the bloodstream.","Absorb, retain"],["Severe or bare in appearance","The stark landscape was devoid of vegetation.","Decorated, lush"],["To emphasize or highlight","The findings underscore the importance of education.","Deemphasize, ignore"],["Never done or known before","The team achieved unprecedented success.","Common, ordinary"],["Ability to work or be successful","The viability of the plan was questioned.","Impracticality, infeasibility"],["Absolutely necessary or important","Water is vital for survival.","Unimportant, unnecessary"],["Influence or power","The celebrity used her clout to support the cause.","Weakness, insignificance"],["To form an idea or plan","She conceived a brilliant idea for the project.","Forget, dismiss"],["To think deeply about something","He contemplated the meaning of life.","Ignore, disregard"],["Based on what is traditionally done","She wore a conventional wedding dress.","Unorthodox, unconventional"],["To confirm or support","The evidence corroborated the witness's testimony.","Contradict, disprove"],["Respect and esteem for others","He showed deference to his elders.","Disrespect, disregard"],["To use up or exhaust resources","The drought depleted the water supply.","Replenish, increase"],["The feeling that something is unworthy","He looked at the messy room with disdain.","Respect, admiration"],["A solemn promise","She took a vow to always help those in need.","Breach, break"],["To become less intense","The storm finally abated after several hours.","Intensify, escalate"],["Sufficient or enough","The resources were adequate for the task.","Inadequate, insufficient"]],[["Comparable in certain respects","The human brain is analogous to a computer.","Dissimilar, unrelated"],["The top or highest part of something","He reached the apex of his career.","Base, bottom"],["Able to express ideas clearly","She is very articulate when explaining her ideas.","Inarticulate, unclear"],["A confident statement of fact or belief","His assertion was supported by evidence.","Denial, doubt"],["Unconventional and slightly strange","His eccentric behavior made him stand out.","Conventional, normal"],["Fluent and persuasive in speaking","Her speech was both eloquent and moving.","Inarticulate, clumsy"],["The state of being fierce or violent","The lion attacked with ferocity.","Gentleness, mildness"],["To grow or develop in a healthy way","The plants flourished in the rich soil.","Wither, decline"],["Deserving or causing public disgrace","The ignominious defeat embarrassed the team.","Honorable, respectable"],["Fairness and lack of bias","The judge's impartiality was unquestionable.","Bias, prejudice"],["A subtle difference in meaning","The artist captured the nuances of light beautifully.","Obviousness, bluntness"],["More important than anything else","Safety is of paramount importance.","Trivial, unimportant"],["To provide evidence for","The claims were substantiated by scientific research.","Disprove, refute"],["Full of or swarming with","The river was teeming with fish.","Empty, barren"],["To justify or necessitate","His actions did not warrant such harsh punishment.","Disqualify, invalidate"],["Open to more than one interpretation","His answer was ambiguous and unclear.","Clear, obvious"],["Well-meaning and kind","The benevolent donor helped many families.","Malevolent, cruel"],["A noisy fight in a crowd","A brawl broke out in the bar.","Peace, harmony"],["Conciseness of expression","The essay's brevity was appreciated by the judges.","Lengthiness, verbosity"],["Relating to a city or town","She is involved in many civic activities.","Private, individual"],["Smug and self-satisfied","He became complacent after achieving his goals.","Ambitious, striving"],["Careful and persistent work","His diligence earned him a promotion.","Neglect, laziness"],["The action of diversifying","Diversification of investments reduces risk.","Uniformity, sameness"],["To provide with a quality or gift","He was endowed with exceptional talent.","Deprive, strip"],["The practicality of something","The feasibility of the plan was evaluated.","Impracticality, impossibility"],["Forming a necessary base","Equality is a fundamental principle of democracy.","Superficial, secondary"],["Impossible to satisfy","She had an insatiable curiosity for knowledge.","Satisfied, content"],["Impossible to bring into agreement","Their differences were irreconcilable.","Compatible, harmonious"],["Intending harm","The malicious rumor hurt her reputation.","Kind, benevolent"],["The highest point","Winning the championship was the pinnacle of his career.","Bottom, low point"],["Seeming reasonable or probable","Her explanation seemed plausible.","Unbelievable, implausible"],["To suggest something as a basis for reasoning","The scientist postulated a new theory.","Reject, deny"],["In a restricted or infrequent manner","Use the medicine sparingly to avoid side effects.","Excessively, liberally"]]],"st":[[["Abundant in supply or quantity","She had copious notes from the lecture.","Scarce, sparse"],["Occurring irregularly or at intervals","The rain was sporadic throughout the day.","Consistent, regular"],["To change the order or arrangement of something","The teacher asked us to transpose the rows and columns.","Organize, maintain"],["To express sorrow or regret","He lamented the loss of his childhood home.","Celebrate, rejoice"],["To involve or require as a necessary part","This project entails a lot of research and dedication.","Exclude, omit"],["Of great importance or significance","The signing of the treaty was a momentous occasion.","Insignificant, trivial"],["Clean and unspoiled; in its original state","The forest remains pristine despite nearby urbanization.","Dirty, corrupted"],["To make narrower by pressing together","The snake constricted its prey tightly.","Expand, release"],["Vague, unclear, or ill-defined","His plans for the future remain nebulous.","Clear, distinct"],["To support or strengthen something","The new law is intended to buttress economic growth.","Weaken, undermine"],["To disprove or argue against","He refuted the allegations with solid evidence.","Support, confirm"],["To confirm or give support to","The scientist corroborated the findings with additional data.","Contradict, oppose"],["Thorough and attentive to detail","Her scrupulous approach ensures accuracy in her work.","Careless, negligent"],["To clear someone of blame or suspicion","New evidence vindicated the wrongly accused man.","Blame, incriminate"],["To prevent something from happening","Heavy rain precluded us from going hiking.","Enable, permit"],["To reject or disown something","He repudiated the accusations during the trial.","Accept, embrace"],["To make less severe, serious, or painful","Measures were taken to mitigate the effects of climate change.","Aggravate, intensify"],["Unusually large or oversized","The outsized package couldn't fit through the door.","Small, undersized"],["Easily noticeable or capable of being felt","There was a palpable sense of excitement in the air.","Subtle, intangible"],["To show or demonstrate clearly","The data evinced a clear trend in customer behavior.","Hide, obscure"],["Failed to be noticed or considered","The significance of her contributions was overlooked.","Recognized, acknowledged"],["To emphasize or highlight something","The report accentuated the need for policy reform.","Downplay, de-emphasize"],["To act against something to reduce its effect","The drug counteracted the effects of the poison.","Support, promote"],["Impossible to overcome","The mountain presented an insuperable challenge.","Surmountable, conquerable"],["Beyond criticism; faultless","Her irreproachable character earned her universal respect.","Flawed, reproachable"]],[["The quality of being showy or self-important","Her pretentiousness was apparent in the way she spoke.","Modesty, humility"],["Impossible to avoid or resist","The consequences of his actions were ineluctable.","Avoidable, escapable"],["Open to more than one interpretation; ambiguous","Her reply was equivocal, leaving us uncertain of her intentions.","Clear, definite"],["Not important or significant","The typo in the document was inconsequential to the final decision.","Significant, meaningful"],["Visible signs or expressions of something","The protests were manifestations of widespread discontent.","Concealments, absences"],["Not clearly understood or easily expressed","The explanation was too obscure for most to understand.","Clear, evident"],["To correct or make something right","He tried to rectify his mistakes by apologizing.","Worsen, corrupt"],["To make a bad situation better","Efforts were made to ameliorate the living conditions in the area.","Worsen, exacerbate"],["Impossible to achieve","The peak was deemed unattainable without proper equipment.","Achievable, possible"],["Unnecessary, especially through being more than enough","He spent money on superfluous items he didn't need.","Necessary, essential"],["Without a clearly defined shape or form","The plan was amorphous and lacked clear goals.","Defined, structured"],["Interpreted wrongly","His comments were misconstrued as criticism.","Understood, clarified"],["Excessively expensive; forbidding","The cost of the tickets was prohibitive for most families.","Affordable, accessible"],["To demand or specify as part of an agreement","The contract stipulates the terms of the agreement clearly.","Suggest, imply"],["To bring about or give rise to","The drug can induce drowsiness in some patients.","Prevent, hinder"],["To cause or give rise to a feeling or situation","Their actions engendered trust among the team members.","Suppress, discourage"],["Scattered across a wide area","The seeds were dispersed by the wind.","Concentrated, gathered"],["To take the place of something, often by force","The new product aims to supplant its predecessor.","Retain, preserve"],["Severe or strict in manner or appearance","Her austere demeanor was softened by her kindness.","Luxurious, indulgent"],["Fair and impartial","The decision was equitable to all parties involved.","Unfair, biased"],["To make something greater by adding to it","The team augmented their resources to meet the deadline.","Reduce, decrease"],["Based on or in accordance with what is traditionally done","Her dress style was very conventional, fitting societal norms.","Unorthodox, unconventional"],["Distinctive or peculiar to an individual","His idiosyncratic habits made him memorable.","Common, typical"],["To come together to form one whole","The rivers coalesce into a large delta.","Separate, divide"],["A brief summary or general overview","The report provided a concise synopsis of the findings.","Expansion, elaboration"]],[["Existing in large quantities; plentiful","The harvest was abundant this year.","Scarce, insufficient"],["The quality of being rough or crude","The coarseness of his language offended the audience.","Refinement, delicacy"],["Adhering to traditional beliefs or practices","He follows orthodox religious practices.","Unorthodox, unconventional"],["To echo or resound repeatedly","The sound of the explosion reverberated through the valley.","Muffle, silence"],["Relating to a town or city and its governance","Municipal elections will be held next month.","Private, rural"],["To move back and forth or to influence someone's opinion","The wind swayed the trees gently.","Steady, stabilize"],["Not genuine or false","The spurious claims were dismissed by the court.","Authentic, genuine"],["In a manner showing excessive generosity or leniency","She indulgently allowed her child to stay up late.","Strictly, harshly"],["To observe or see something","We beheld the stunning view from the mountain.","Ignore, overlook"],["To satisfy fully or to excess","The buffet satiated everyone's hunger.","Deprive, starve"],["The act of gathering or assembling","The convening of the council was announced yesterday.","Dismissing, dispersing"],["To view something or someone as perfect","She tends to idealize her past experiences.","Criticize, devalue"],["Not conforming to established doctrines or beliefs","His heterodox views often spark debates.","Orthodox, conformist"],["Impossible to deny or disprove","The evidence presented was irrefutable.","Refutable, questionable"],["To regard with great respect or reverence","They venerate the founder of their community.","Disrespect, despise"],["Involving great effort or difficulty","Climbing the mountain was an arduous task.","Easy, effortless"],["Requiring much effort or energy","The strenuous workout left him exhausted.","Effortless, relaxed"],["Not pretentious; simple and sincere","Her unpretentious manner made her approachable.","Pretentious, pompous"],["Capable of being satisfied","He is easily satiable with small portions.","Insatiable, unquenchable"],["Not in harmony with surroundings or expectations","The modern decor was incongruous with the ancient building.","Harmonious, fitting"],["Occurring or appearing again periodically","The symptoms were recurrent every few weeks.","Irregular, singular"],["Grand and impressive in appearance","The imposing mansion stood at the edge of the cliff.","Modest, unimpressive"],["Commanding respect due to age or dignity","The venerable professor was admired by all.","Modern, dishonorable"],["Unpredictable or inconsistent","His erratic behavior confused his colleagues.","Consistent, stable"],["Well-meaning and kind","Her benevolent actions benefited the entire village.","Malevolent, cruel"]],[["The act of generating revenue from something","She is monetizing her social media content.","Demonetizing, ignoring"],["Assessing or evaluating the value of something","The art dealer spent hours appraising the painting.","Neglecting, ignoring"],["Leaving no doubt; clear and unambiguous","The instructions were unequivocal and left no room for doubt.","Ambiguous, uncertain"],["Replaced or succeeded by something newer","The old rules have been superseded by modern regulations.","Retained, preserved"],["Shared or similar to others","He has much in common with his colleagues.","Unrelated, unique"],["Working jointly with others","The project was a collaboration with several universities.","Isolation, opposition"],["A backup or supply held for future use","She kept a reserve of supplies for emergencies.","Depletion, emptiness"],["To hinder or obstruct progress","The bad weather impeded their progress.","Facilitate, assist"],["To be worthy of something","He deserves recognition for his efforts.","Deny, unworthy"],["Focused on individual interests or independence","Her individualistic approach set her apart from the group.","Communal, collective"],["The act of comparing or examining similarities and differences","A comparison of the two products showed significant differences.","Contrast, difference"],["Of the same kind or similar nature","The neighborhood is remarkably homogeneous in its culture.","Diverse, heterogeneous"],["To take up space or time","They occupy the house during the summer months.","Vacate, abandon"],["Mutually reliant on each other","The two species are interdependent for survival.","Independent, separate"],["A person who actively opposes something","The antagonist in the story plotted against the hero.","Ally, supporter"],["To produce or give way","The fields yield a good harvest each year.","Resist, refuse"],["To imitate or strive to equal","He tried to emulate his mentor's success.","Neglect, shun"],["To be evident or appear in something","Her leadership skills were manifest in every project she undertook.","Hidden, obscure"],["Close examination or observation","The documents were under close scrutiny.","Neglect, overlook"],["Stubborn or refusing to yield","She remained unyielding in her stance.","Flexible, yielding"],["To communicate or make known","The author conveyed a powerful message in the book.","Suppress, withhold"],["High status or reputation","The award added to her prestige in the field.","Disrepute, dishonor"],["Very weak or insubstantial","The bridge's tenuous connection to the land worried the engineers.","Strong, substantial"],["To divide or share","The two partners decided to partiate the profits.","Consolidate, hoard"],["Found everywhere; omnipresent","Smartphones are ubiquitous in modern society.","Rare, uncommon"]],[["Hostile feelings or attitudes toward someone or something","The animosities toward the policy were evident in the protests.","Friendliness, goodwill"],["Strong, healthy, and resilient","The robust economy weathered the crisis.","Weak, frail"],["Present everywhere at the same time","The influence of technology is omnipresent in modern life.","Rare, localized"],["To separate or move in different directions","The paths diverge at the edge of the forest.","Converge, meet"],["To examine something closely and critically","She scrutinized the document for any errors.","Ignore, neglect"],["To become knowledgeable about something","He familiarized himself with the new software before starting work.","Disregard, overlook"],["To take the place of something","The new model will replace the outdated version.","Retain, preserve"],["To watch or monitor carefully","They observed the birds through binoculars.","Disregard, ignore"],["To refuse or dismiss something","She rejected the offer without hesitation.","Accept, approve"],["The quality of being precise or accurate","The exactitude of the calculations impressed everyone.","Inaccuracy, imprecision"],["To predict or infer based on known information","From the data, we can extrapolate future trends.","Misinterpret, miscalculate"],["To cause someone to feel sudden shock or surprise","The loud noise startled the baby.","Calm, reassure"],["A natural liking for or attraction to something","She has a strong affinity for classical music.","Aversion to, dislike"],["Uncertainty or doubt about something","His hesitancy about the decision was understandable.","Certainty, confidence"],["To divide or separate into parts","The partition divided the room into two sections.","Unite, combine"],["Inappropriate or unfavorable","The untoward comment caused an awkward silence.","Favorable, appropriate"],["To display or show a quality or feeling","Her talent manifested itself early in childhood.","Hide, conceal"],["To explain the meaning of something","The dictionary defines the word clearly.","Confuse, obscure"],["To form a mental image of something","She visualized her goals vividly before taking action.","Ignore, dismiss"],["Resemblances or comparable aspects with something","Their artwork shows similarities with the Impressionist style.","Differences from, divergence from"],["Instances that demonstrate or illustrate something","The teacher provided examples of good essays.","Counterexamples, exceptions"],["A sign or evidence of something","The sudden drop in temperature was an indication of the coming storm.","Absence of, lack of"],["To approach or catch up with someone or something","The runner was gaining on the leader in the final lap.","Falling behind, losing ground"],["Easily broken or damaged","The fragile vase shattered when it fell.","Durable, sturdy"],["Unwilling or hesitant to do something","He was reluctant to share his personal information.","Willing, eager"]],[["Uncertainty or doubt in making a decision","Her hesitancy to accept the job offer was evident.","Confidence, certainty"],["To carve or shape something from a material","The artist hewed a sculpture out of the marble.","Destroy, dismantle"],["To bring people together for a meeting or assembly","The committee will convene next Monday to discuss the issue.","Disperse, scatter"],["To leave a place, making it empty","They had to vacate the premises immediately.","Occupy, fill"],["To imitate or copy someone's behavior or actions","The child mimicked her teacher's voice perfectly.","Original, create"],["Easily noticeable or attracting attention","Her conspicuous outfit drew everyone's attention.","Inconspicuous, hidden"],["To increase in power, status, or wealth","The politician sought to aggrandize his reputation.","Diminish, belittle"],["Impossible to replace or substitute","The handmade artifact was deemed irreplaceable.","Replaceable, expendable"],["Deviating from what is standard or expected","His anomalous behavior raised suspicion.","Normal, standard"],["Having no basis in fact; groundless","The rumors were unfounded and dismissed by the authorities.","Justified, proven"],["A machine for mixing or blending substances","She used a blender to prepare the smoothie.","Separator, divider"],["Evoking strong emotion or feeling","The movie's ending was deeply affecting.","Unmoving, unemotional"],["A person or thing that comes before another","The Wright brothers were precursors to modern aviation.","Successor, follower"],["Confused or bewildered","She looked bemused as she read the strange letter.","Clear-headed, focused"],["To adjust or mark something to ensure accuracy","The technician calibrated the instrument before use.","Disarrange, misalign"],["Filled with bitter criticism or malice","His vitriolic remarks offended everyone at the meeting.","Mild, pleasant"],["Unfairly prejudiced for or against something","The biased referee favored the home team.","Unbiased, impartial"],["Asserting opinions as undeniably true","The leader's dogmatic views alienated his followers.","Open-minded, flexible"],["Calm, peaceful, or untroubled","The serene lake was a perfect spot for meditation.","Chaotic, turbulent"],["Lacking originality; obvious and boring","The novel was criticized for its banal plot.","Unique, extraordinary"],["Implied or understood without being stated","Her agreement was implicit in her actions.","Explicit, stated"],["A natural consequence or result","A corollary of economic growth is increased environmental impact.","Cause, antecedent"],["Happened at the same time as something else","The meeting coincided with the CEO's visit.","Differed from, contrasted with"],["Conformity to rules or law; validity","The court questioned the legitimacy of the new law.","Illegitimacy, invalidity"],["Not producing the desired effect","The plan was ineffectual in solving the problem.","Effective, successful"]],[["Clever, inventive, and resourceful","Her ingenious solution to the problem impressed everyone.","Unimaginative, dull"],["Showing great attention to detail","He is meticulous about keeping his desk organized.","Careless, sloppy"],["The ability to evoke a sense of harmony or sympathy","The resonance of the music filled the hall.","Dissonance, discord"],["The quality of being watchful and alert","The guards maintained vigilance throughout the night.","Negligence, inattentiveness"],["Having the opposite effect of what was intended","Arguing during the meeting was counterproductive.","Effective, beneficial"],["An inconsistency or lack of compatibility","There was a discrepancy between the two accounts.","Agreement, consistency"],["A disagreement or argument","They had a dispute over the ownership of the land.","Agreement, harmony"],["Careful consideration or discussion","After much deliberation, they decided to accept the offer.","Haste, impulsiveness"],["General agreement among a group","The team reached a consensus on the strategy.","Disagreement, conflict"],["Rough or lacking refinement","His coarse manners made others uncomfortable.","Refined, elegant"],["The act of trying to influence decisions, especially in politics","The company spent millions on lobbying for the new law.","Opposing, resisting"],["To reduce or take away the value of something","Criticism did not detract from her achievements.","Enhance, add"],["Believing that people are motivated by self-interest","He has a cynical view of politics.","Trusting, optimistic"],["Not clear or sharply defined","The photo was too indistinct to recognize anyone.","Distinct, clear"],["A subtle difference in meaning, expression, or sound","She appreciated the nuances of his argument.","Obvious, simplicity"],["Comprehensive and thorough","The report provided an exhaustive analysis of the data.","Superficial, incomplete"],["Made greater in size, amount, or value","The features of the app were augmented in the new update.","Reduced, diminished"],["Quoted as evidence or support","She cited multiple studies to support her argument.","Ignored, omitted"],["Overused and unoriginal","The movie was full of clichéd dialogues.","Original, innovative"],["Agreement or harmony","There was a strong congruence between their goals.","Incompatibility, conflict"],["Restricted or limited","His constrained movements indicated he was in pain.","Unrestricted, free"],["Believable and trustworthy","The evidence presented was credible.","Unreliable, doubtful"],["Traditional or habitual","It is customary to remove your shoes before entering.","Uncommon, unusual"],["Able to make decisions quickly and effectively","Her decisive leadership saved the company.","Indecisive, hesitant"],["Ran away quickly from danger or pursuit","The thief fled the scene before the police arrived.","Stayed, lingered"]],[["Diverse in content or character","The city has a heterogeneous population.","Homogeneous, uniform"],["Absolutely necessary or required","It is imperative to finish the project on time.","Optional, unnecessary"],["To make improvements or do better than before","She worked hard to improve on her previous performance.","Worsen, degrade"],["Closely linked or unable to be separated from","The issue is inextricable from larger social problems.","Separate from, unrelated to"],["The act of explaining the meaning of something","His interpretation of the law was controversial.","Misinterpretation, confusion"],["Belonging naturally; essential","Honesty is intrinsic to his character.","Extrinsic, nonessential"],["Extremely valuable or useful","The document was of invaluable importance to the case.","Worthless, trivial"],["To block or prevent something","The fallen tree obstructed the road.","Facilitate, unblock"],["A typical example or pattern of something","The model serves as a paradigm for future designs.","Anomaly, deviation"],["To spread through or penetrate","The smell of flowers permeated the room.","Isolate, block"],["To copy or reproduce something exactly","They replicated the experiment to confirm the results.","Alter, distort"],["Lower in rank or position","As a subordinate, he reported to the department head.","Superior, chief"],["To put an end to something by force","The government suppressed the uprising.","Encourage, promote"],["Having flat, leveled surfaces for cultivation","The terraced hills were perfect for farming.","Uneven, sloped"],["To reduce the importance or value of something","He discounted her concerns as insignificant.","Acknowledge, emphasize"],["To publicly declare something to be wrong or evil","The journalist denounced the corruption scandal.","Praise, commend"],["No longer existing or functioning","The factory is now defunct and abandoned.","Operational, active"],["To make something appear larger","The microscope magnifies small details.","Reduce, minimize"],["To make an unpleasant feeling less intense","He tried to assuage her fears with reassuring words.","Aggravate, intensify"],["To assign or appoint someone for a task","She was designated as the team leader.","Ignore, neglect"],["The act of making concessions to maintain peace","The policy of appeasement failed to prevent the war.","Confrontation, resistance"],["To increase in size, strength, or effect","The speaker amplified his voice using a microphone.","Diminish, weaken"],["To refrain or hold back voluntarily","He abstained from voting in the election.","Participate, indulge"],["Open to multiple interpretations","The ambiguous statement left everyone confused.","Clear, definite"],["Kind and gentle","The medication has benign side effects.","Harmful, malignant"]],[["Unnecessary or unwarranted","The movie was criticized for its gratuitous violence.","Necessary, justified"],["Based on or involving a hypothesis","This is just a hypothetical scenario, not reality.","Factual, actual"],["Forbidden by law or rules","The sale of illicit goods is prohibited.","Legal, permitted"],["To find a way around an obstacle or rule","He tried to circumvent the rules by using loopholes.","Follow, comply"],["Dependent on something else","His attendance is contingent to the approval of his supervisor.","Independent, certain"],["Required to do something","She felt obliged to help her friend.","Freed, unbound"],["To hinder or block progress","The ongoing strike stymied their plans for production.","Facilitate, assist"],["To criticize unfairly","He denigrated her achievements out of jealousy.","Praise, commend"],["Highly skilled or proficient at something","She is adept at solving complex puzzles.","Inept, clumsy"],["To make something invalid or void","The new evidence nullifies the previous claims.","Validate, enforce"],["Taking unfair advantage of something or someone","He was exploiting the system for his own benefit.","Supporting, respecting"],["Not taking something seriously","She was lighthearted about the minor mistake.","Serious, concerned"],["To surpass or exceed","The athlete outstripped his competitors in the final lap.","Lag behind, fail"],["To belittle or speak disrespectfully of","He disparaged their efforts despite their hard work.","Compliment, admire"],["To give something a sense of worth or nobility","The medal dignified his years of service.","Degrade, demean"],["Acceptable to taste or mind","The dish was both palatable and visually appealing.","Unpleasant, unacceptable"],["Unpleasant or unacceptable to taste or mind","The unpalatable truth was hard to accept.","Tolerable, acceptable"],["To provide with sustenance or support","The gardener nourished the plants with care.","Deprive, neglect"],["Understood by few; mysterious or secret","The arcane rituals were known only to the priests.","Common, well-known"],["To place side by side for comparison","The artist juxtaposed modern elements with classical designs.","Separate, isolate"],["High regard or respect","She is held in high esteem by her colleagues.","Disdain, disrespect"],["An opening, gap, or hole","Light filtered through the narrow aperture in the wall.","Closure, seal"],["Word unclear or requires clarification","Definition for 'Meteged' is unclear.","Organized, systematic"],["Lacking any obvious organization","The decorations were arranged in a haphazard manner.","Continuation, permanence"],["To give relief","The threatened hospitals could now be reprieved","Punishment, penalty"]],[["To light up or clarify something","The lantern illuminated the dark room.","Darken, obscure"],["An opinion or conclusion formed without complete information","His conjecture about the outcome proved to be correct.","Fact, certainty"],["Something unusual or peculiar","Her quirky style was considered an oddity in the office.","Normality, regularity"],["A remarkable concurrence of events or circumstances","It was a coincidence that they met on the same flight.","Causation, intentionality"],["An event or occurrence","The incident was reported to the authorities.","Routine, plan"],["Likely to cause disagreement or argument","The contentious debate lasted for hours.","Agreeable, amicable"],["The quality of being honest and genuine","Her sincerity was evident in her heartfelt apology.","Deceit, insincerity"],["Contrary to facts or reality","The counterfactual scenario explored what might have been.","Factual, actual"],["Comparable in certain respects","The structure of the two systems is analogous.","Dissimilar, unrelated"],["Fragile, sensitive, or requiring careful handling","The delicate vase shattered when it fell.","Rough, sturdy"],["Based on long-established customs or practices","The festival is rooted in traditional practices.","Modern, innovative"],["Never done or known before","The scientist made an unprecedented discovery.","Conventional, precedented"],["Calm, serene, and free from disturbance","The tranquil lake was a perfect spot for relaxation.","Chaotic, turbulent"],["The ability to produce the desired effect","The efficacy of the drug was confirmed in clinical trials.","Ineffectiveness, inefficacy"],["Free from conflict or disturbance","They enjoyed a peaceful afternoon in the park.","Hostile, turbulent"],["Optimistic or positive, especially in a difficult situation","Despite the challenges, he remained sanguine about the future.","Pessimistic, negative"],["Existing only in theory or as a concept","The notional value of the property exceeded expectations.","Real, concrete"],["The action of setting boundaries or limits","The river served as a natural demarcation between the two regions.","Integration, union"],["Deep or intense, especially in meaning or impact","Her speech had a profound impact on the audience.","Superficial, shallow"],["Lacking a clear plan or purpose","The student's desultory approach to studying led to poor results.","Purposeful, organized"],["Having a dislike or distrust of humankind","The misanthropic character preferred solitude.","Philanthropic, trusting"],["Existing in name only; insignificant","The fee was only nominal and barely covered the costs.","Substantial, significant"],["Resisting authority or control","The recalcitrant teenager refused to follow the rules.","Compliant, obedient"],["To mediate or intervene on behalf of another","She interceded to resolve the conflict between her friends.","Ignore, neglect"],["To gather or collect a large amount of something","Over the years, he amassed a large collection of rare books.","Disperse, scatter"]],[["Not easily noticed or attracting attention","The shy student remained inconspicuous in the crowd.","Conspicuous, noticeable"],["The quality of behaving or speaking in a careful way","She handled the sensitive matter with great discretion.","Indiscretion, recklessness"],["Being truly or very much so; genuine","The cake was a veritable masterpiece of baking.","False, fake"],["Clever or skillful in using the hands or mind","He is adroit at solving complex problems.","Clumsy, inept"],["New or original","The scientist introduced a novel approach to the experiment.","Old, traditional"],["Lacking social grace or sensitivity","His gauche comments embarrassed everyone at the table.","Graceful, polished"],["To mix or combine into a single substance or entity","The recipe calls for a blend of spices.","Separate, isolate"],["The act of moving to a new place","The company's relocation to the city was announced.","Stagnation, immobility"],["The process of grouping items based on shared characteristics","The classification of plants helps in their study.","Disorganization, randomness"],["Unreasonably high or excessive","The price of the designer bag was exorbitant.","Reasonable, affordable"],["Not justified or necessary","The complaints were based on unwarranted assumptions.","Justified, necessary"],["To combine two or more things into one","He mistakenly conflated the two ideas in his argument.","Separate, divide"],["Reformed or restored to its original state","The reconstituted soup tasted as fresh as homemade.","Ruined, destroyed"],["In a manner that is done together","They jointly signed the agreement.","Individually, separately"],["To give or bestow something","The teacher imparted valuable knowledge to her students.","Withhold, keep"]],[["To restore or improve something, especially a building","They decided to renovate the old house, giving it a modern look.","Deteriorate"],["The act of getting something back","He spent hours retrieving his lost phone from the river.","Losing"],["Hesitant or stopping often","His halting speech made it clear he was nervous.","Fluent"],["A distinctive feature or characteristic","Attention to detail is the hallmark of a great writer.","Atypical trait"],["To carry, endure, or tolerate","She had to bear the weight of responsibility alone.","Avoid"],["Hidden from view or knowledge","The treasure was concealed from the pirates in a secret cave.","Revealed to"],["Criticized or mocked using satire","The politician was satirized in the latest comedy sketch.","Praised"],["To go beyond limits, often excessively","The company overreached by expanding too quickly and went bankrupt.","Stay within bounds"],["Drawing out a reaction or response","His joke was effective in eliciting laughter from the crowd.","Suppressing"],["Taking advantage of a situation","She is capitalizing on the popularity of sustainable fashion.","Ignoring"],["Makes something seem less important","His achievements overshadowed those of his colleagues.","Highlights"],["The way something is received or welcomed","The reception of the new policy was largely negative.","Rejection of"],["To surpass or outshine something","His talent eclipsed everyone else's on the team.","Inferior to"],["To be the perfect example of something","She epitomized grace and kindness in her speech.","Contradicted"],["Suitable or well-timed for something","This is an opportune moment for launching a new product.","Inopportune for"],["Lower in rank or position compared to something","The assistant’s role is subordinate to the manager's.","Superior to"],["Informed or made aware of something","She was apprised of the latest company policies.","Unaware of"],["Calmed or soothed by something","The angry customer was placated by a sincere apology.","Agitated by"],["Given as an honor or gift","The highest award was bestowed on the veteran scientist.","Taken away from"],["Created or caused by something","The destruction was wrought by a massive hurricane.","Undone by"],["Lack of interest or concern about something","His apathy toward politics surprised his friends.","Passion for"],["Fairness, without bias","Judges must act with impartiality in all cases.","Bias"],["Mixed or contradictory feelings about something","He felt ambivalence about moving to a new city.","Certainty"],["To take advantage of something, often unfairly","The company was accused of exploiting its workers.","Respect"],["To perceive or recognize something clearly","She could discern the truth behind his words.","Overlook"]],[["Without equal; unmatched","Her unrivaled talent won her the championship.","inferior"],["Unchangeable; fixed","The immutable laws of physics govern the universe.","changeable"],["Combined or united","The two companies amalgamated to form a larger corporation.","separated"],["Formally announced or made public","The new policy was promulgated through an official statement.","concealed"],["To predict or prophesy","The oracle could foretell the kingdom’s future.","conceal"],["Attempting to impress by appearing more important","His pretentious speech annoyed the audience.","humble"],["To assume beforehand","The theory presupposes a basic understanding of math.","disprove"],["To intervene on behalf of another","She interceded to resolve the conflict between friends.","avoid"],["Done together by two or more parties","They jointly organized the community event.","individually"],["Applied to past events","The law was applied retroactively to past cases.","prospectively"],["Strictness or thoroughness","The rigor of the training program prepared them well.","leniency"],["The state of being unknown or unclear","The poet lived in obscurity for most of her life.","fame"],["Having foresight or imagination","His visionary ideas transformed the industry.","shortsighted"],["Using irony to mock or convey contempt","Her sarcastic remark hurt his feelings.","sincere"],["To hinder or obstruct","Heavy traffic impeded their journey.","assist"],["Mutual exchange","Their friendship was built on reciprocity.","selfishness"],["The act of sticking together","Team cohesion improved their performance.","division"],["Causing or likely to cause disagreement","The contentious debate divided the group.","agreeable"],["Unreasonably high or excessive","The exorbitant price of the car shocked buyers.","reasonable"],["Justified or necessary","Her reaction was warranted given the situation.","unjustified"],["Resolved through an intermediary","The dispute was mediated by a neutral party.","direct"],["To dominate or make less important","His success overshadowed his earlier failures.","highlight"],["Continuing to exist or endure","Her persisting efforts finally paid off.","ceasing"],["Difficult to carry out or fulfill","The burdensome task exhausted the team.","easy"],["Thin or lacking excess","The lean budget forced them to cut expenses.","excessive"]],[["Based on illusion; not real or true; deceptive","The magician’s tricks gave the audience an illusory sense of danger.","Real"],["Impossible to explain or understand","The sudden disappearance of the keys was inexplicable.","Explainable"],["To insult or belittle; also to write down","He felt embarrassed when his friend put him down in front of others.","Compliment"],["To organize so parts work together effectively","The teams must coordinate their efforts to succeed.","Disorganize"],["Showing concern for others' feelings","She is always considerate toward her classmates.","Inconsiderate"],["A person learning a trade from a skilled employer","The apprentice learned woodworking techniques from his master.","Expert"],["To speed up or facilitate","The manager expedited the approval process.","Delay"],["Fertility or ability to produce abundantly","The region’s soil is known for its natural fecundity.","Barrenness"],["The quality of being convenient and practical despite possibly being improper","He chose expediency over honesty to solve the issue quickly.","Integrity"],["To give a brief statement of the main points","The teacher asked him to summarize the chapter in two sentences.","Elaborate"],["Resistance to change in motion or condition","The project remained stuck due to the team’s inertia.","Momentum"],["Treating serious issues with inappropriate humor","His facetious remarks during the meeting annoyed everyone.","Serious"],["A person who manages or looks after something","The steward ensured that all guests were comfortable.","Neglector"],["To publicly denounce or criticize","Many activists decried the unfair new policy.","Praise"],["To become fully aware of something; to achieve","She realized her mistake and corrected it immediately.","Ignore"],["To remove or take away; to retreat or pull back","He decided to withdraw his application from the program.","Advance"],["To focus all attention or effort on something","He needed complete silence to concentrate on his homework.","Distract"],["The ability to make decisions quickly and firmly","Her decisiveness helped the team avoid unnecessary delays.","Indecision"],["To open by removing bolts or fasteners","He unbolted the door and stepped outside quietly.","Fasten"],["Having a pleasant melody or tune","The singer’s melodic voice captivated the entire audience.","Harsh"],["To show or display","The museum will exhibit ancient artifacts this summer.","Hide"],["To openly resist or refuse to obey","The protesters continued to defy the curfew.","Obey"],["Attempting to impress by affecting greater importance","His pretentious tone annoyed everyone in the room.","Modest"],["To cause something to start or happen","The loud noise triggered the alarm instantly.","Prevent"],["To calm or relieve pain or distress","Warm tea can help soothe a sore throat.","Aggravate"]],[["High respect; to regard with great respect and esteem","I’d be honored if you didn't tell my boss I’m wearing slippers.","Shame, disgrace; dishonor"],["To remove or take away; to retreat or pull back","I had to withdraw my proposal after everyone laughed.","Remain, maintain"],["To guide or control the direction of something","You can't steer a shopping cart that well.","Follow, drift, misdirect"],["Public disagreement or heated discussion within a topic","The biggest controversy in my house is the thermostat setting.","Agreement, harmony"],["The state of being introduced to or affected by something","My only exposure to sunshine is when I check the mail.","Concealment, hiding"],["Reliance on or need for something or someone","My dependence on snacks is becoming a problem.","Independence, freedom"],["Progress or development in a particular area","The latest advancement in science proves that snacks cure almost everything.","Stagnation, decline"],["To extend the duration of something","My cat attempts to prolong mealtime by pretending she forgot how to chew for exactly three minutes after every bite.","Shorten, abridge"],["To calm or relieve pain or distress","I only use ice cream to soothe my emotional turbulence, which is why I require six scoops daily.","Aggravate, disturb"],["Disgusted or shocked by something","I was revolted by the sheer amount of cilantro in my dinner.","Delighted, pleased"],["Higher in rank, status, or quality","My dog thinks her stick is superior to all other sticks.","Inferior, lower"],["The process or result of joining two or more things together.","My dinner was a terrible fusion of leftovers and bad ideas.","Separation, division"],["The act of sending someone away or rejecting something","My cat gave me a cold dismissal when I offered wet food.","Acceptance"],["A detailed analysis and assessment","My only critique of this cookie is that it isn't infinite.","Praise, approval"],["The act of making something simpler or easier to understand","My taxes need radical simplification.","Complication"],["To say something again or differently","Just to restate, I need more pizza.","Conceal, suppress"],["To discover or identify the presence of something","I could detect a hint of failure in my burnt toast.","Miss, overlook"],["To officially register as a member or participant","He tried to enroll in the class, but his credit card rebelled.","Withdraw, drop out"],["The importance, worth, or usefulness of something","I place high value on my ability to nap anywhere, anytime.","Worthlessness, uselessness"],["To pay no attention to, ignore","I tend to disregard any email that starts with the phrase, \"As per my last email...\"","Acknowledge, heed"],["To show or exhibit","My neighbor loves to display his impressive ability to burn water.","Hide, conceal"],["Not related or applicable to something","My love life is completely irrelevant to the plot of this romantic comedy.","Relevant to, connected to"],["Strongly attracted or fascinated by something","I was captivated by a shiny pebble for ten whole minutes.","Bored by, repulsed by"],["Damaged or impaired by age or use, old-fashioned","My favorite joke is so timeworn that it now requires an historical footnote.","Brand new, fresh"],["An impressive or unusual sight or display","My morning routine is a bizarre spectacle.","Dullness, boredom"]],[["The process of making a copy or duplicate of something","Rabbits treat reproduction like a hobby.","Sterility, extinction"],["Something that changes appearance to hide identity","My cat's disguise was just a napkin.","Revelation, exposure"],["Lasting for a long time, durable","His bad tie proved sadly enduring.","Temporary, ephemeral"],["Limited to a particular group, not shared","Only famous cats get exclusive clubs.","Inclusive, shared"],["Not sure or definite, doubtful","The forecast for raining frogs felt uncertain.","Certain, sure"],["Able to convince or influence someone","The baby's cries were highly persuasive.","Doubtful, unconvincing"],["To come before in time or order","Chaos always seems to precede my diet.","Follow, succeed"],["Not changing, constant","My dinner menu is sadly unvarying: pizza.","Variable, diverse, changing"],["To give or feel in return, respond mutually","I should reciprocate that high-five.","Refuse, ignore"],["To add notes or comments to a text or diagram","Please annotate the silly doodle with notes.","Delete, transcribe"],["To make equal or uniform","We must equalize the cookie distribution now!","Unbalance, disparage"],["Strong and durable; difficult to break or deal with","Grandma's burnt toast was amazingly tough.","Fragile, weak"],["Extremely ugly or unpleasant","That purple plaid shirt is truly hideous.","Beautiful, lovely"],["Impossible to solve or fix","Their argument about pizza toppings was utterly irresolvable.","Solvable, resolvable"],["Containing opposing or conflicting statements or ideas","Saying \"I love silence\" loudly is self-contradictory.","Consistent logical"],["To persuade someone to believe or do something","I will convince my dog that bath time is fun.","Dissuade, discourage"],["To divert attention away from something","I used a squirrel to distract the guard.","Concentrate, engage"],["To give evidence or bear witness, especially in legal contexts","I must testify that my cat stole the snacks.","Deny, repudiate"],["A serious disagreement or argument","There was intense conflict over the last donut.","Agreement, consensus"],["To make fun of or ridicule","Don't mock my incredibly bad dancing.","Praise, compliment"],["Showing no pity or understanding toward someone or something","The drill sergeant was highly unsympathetic to my late nap.","Compassionate, kind"],["Not taking sides; unbiased or impartial","I try to be neutral about coffee versus tea.","Biased, opinionated"],["Causing or speeding up a reaction or change","Coffee is key to catalyzing my morning work.","Slowing, inhibiting"],["Done by choice or free will, without being forced","I voluntarily agreed to eat the last slice.","Compulsorily, involuntarily"],["Gently and with care or affection","She tenderly placed the pizza in the box.","Roughly, harshly"]],[["Discussion aimed at reaching an agreement","The negotiation between the two companies lasted all week.","Disagreement"],["The reason or explanation for something","She provided a strong justification for her absence.","Accusation"],["A firm decision or solution to a problem","He made a resolution to study harder this year.","Indecision"],["Feeling sad because of being alone","She felt lonely after moving to a new city.","Connected"],["No longer remembered","The old tradition has been forgotten by most people.","Remembered"],["Showing diversity or difference","The restaurant offers a varied menu that suits everyone’s tastes.","Uniform"],["Able to be maintained over time without depletion","The company focuses on sustainable energy solutions.","Unsustainable"],["To give official permission","The manager authorized the employee to access confidential files.","Forbid"],["Old-fashioned or obsolete","Many people consider floppy disks outdated technology.","Modern"],["Characterized by constant change or activity","The company operates in a dynamic market environment.","Static"],["Causing enthusiasm or eagerness","The roller coaster ride was exciting for the children.","Boring"],["Causing bewilderment or lack of clarity","The instructions were confusing for beginners.","Clear"],["Not liked or unfavored","His rude behavior made him disliked among peers.","Admired"],["The quality of being new or unusual","The novelty of the gadget attracted many buyers.","Familiarity"],["Lack of depth, either literal or figurative","The shallowness of the argument made it unconvincing.","Depth"],["A feeling of fondness or love","She showed great affection for her younger siblings.","Indifference"],["The ability to return to original shape after stretching; flexibility","The elasticity of the rubber band allowed it to stretch easily.","Rigidity"],["To attract or be relevant to","The advertisement was designed to appeal to young audiences.","Repel"],["To recall or bring back to mind","She tried to remember the details of the conversation.","Forget"],["To recognize or establish as being","The detective was able to identify the suspect.","Confuse"],["To pay no attention to","He chose to ignore the rude comment.","Notice"],["The act of putting something to use for a purpose","His application to the new software improved productivity.","Neglect"],["The way something is understood or interpreted","Public perception of the policy was mostly negative.","Misunderstanding"],["Something given or added to help","Her contribution to the project was greatly appreciated.","Hindrance"],["To stop something from happening","Vaccinations help prevent the spread of disease.",""]],[["To carry out an action or task","The actor will perform in the play tonight.","Fail"],["To separate or disengage","The engineers decided to decouple the two systems for safety.","Connect"],["Important or relevant; also physical substance","The lecture covered material essential for the final exam.","Irrelevant"],["Clearly seen or understood","Her excitement was evident from her smile.","Hidden"],["Regarded as likely or probable","The results were expected based on previous studies.","Unexpected"],["To include or engage","The project will involve students from all grades.","Exclude"],["Specific or special","She had a particular interest in biology.","General"],["Something added to complete or enhance","He took a vitamin supplement every morning.","Reduce"],["Failure to care for properly","The plants died due to neglect.","Care"],["To twist out of shape or misrepresent","The mirror distorted her reflection.","Clarify"],["Detailed examinations or studies of something","The scientist conducted multiple analyses on the samples.","Summaries"],["Happening by chance without apparent cause","Their meeting at the airport was purely coincidental.","Intentional"],["To assess or determine the size, amount, or degree of something","Scientists measure temperature using a thermometer.","Estimate (loosely); Misjudge"],["To change or alter","The prices vary depending on the season.","Stay the same"],["To become or make greater in size or amount","Sales increased significantly during the holiday season.","Decrease"],["To open or reveal something gradually","The story began to unfold as more details emerged.","Fold"],["To take away or eliminate","She removed her name from the volunteer list.","Add"],["The rate at which employees leave and are replaced; also total sales","High turnover made it difficult for the company to maintain stability.","Retention"],["Lack of harmony or agreement; conflict","There was clear dissonance between his words and actions.","Harmony"],["A collection or gathering of things","The report included an aggregation of data from various sources.","Separation"],["Reduction or decrease","There was an abatement in noise after the construction ended.","Increase"],["Avoidance of activity or exertion; laziness","Her indolence kept her from finishing the project on time.","Diligence"],["Casual lack of concern; indifference","His nonchalance during the exam worried the teacher.","Concern"],["A disturbance or disruption","The sudden noise caused a perturbation in the classroom.","Calm"],["To reduce or cut short","The company had to curtail its spending due to budget constraints","Expand"]],[["Not disturbed or troubled by something","The cat was unbothered by the vacuum cleaner dance party.","Disturbed by, concerned about"],["Uncertain or slow to act due to doubt or fear","I was hesitant to try the purple mystery casserole.","Eager, ready, willing"],["A place where things are stored or collected","My brain is a vast repository of silly song lyrics.","Distribution, outlet"],["A formal request, often signed by many people","We signed a petition for more office donuts.","Demand, command"],["An assumption or hypothesis without proof","My supposition that gravity stops on Fridays was false.","Fact, certainty"],["To record or enroll officially","I had to register my sock collection officially.","Delete, unregister"],["To break into small pieces or collapse gradually","The ancient cookie began to crumble immediately.","Solidify, strengthen"],["Understanding or feeling someone else’s feelings, especially sadness","I felt sympathy for the dog who lost his ball.","Indifference, apathy"],["Complete and including everything necessary","The book provided a comprehensive guide to napping.","Incomplete, narrow"],["A feeling or belief that something is wrong or likely true without proof","My suspicion grew after the dog blamed the cat.","Trust, faith"],["something accepted as true without proof","My assumption that I had won the lottery was premature.","Proof, evidence"],["Reaching out or extending in the direction of something","The cat was stretching toward the highest shelf of snacks.","Retreating from, withdrawing from"],["In an awkward or uncoordinated way","I clumsily tripped over the air itself.","Gracefully, skillfully"],["An improvement or increase in quality or value","Putting glitter on my toast was a flavor enhancement.","Reduction, degradation"],["Something made or invented; a lie or falsehood","His story about meeting an alien was a total fabrication.","Truth, reality"],["A surprising or unknown fact made known","The shocking revelation was that my parrot knew algebra.","Concealment, mystery"],["Not qualified or allowed to do or be something","Because I didn't finish my homework, I was ineligible for dessert.","Eligible, qualified"],["Something that does not follow a rule or pattern","My strange, green friend is the one exception to the rule about no guests.","Rule, norm"],["Not aware of or affected by something","My rock was completely insensible to my sad, teary poetry.","Sensitive to, aware of"],["To start or introduce something, such as a project or product","We decided to launch the new product with a massive cake.","Halt, stop"],["To reduce something to the smallest possible amount or degree","We must minimize the distractions before the test.","Maximize, increase"],["To represent or stand for something else","The purple feather seemed to symbolize bad luck and bad fashion.","State, contradict"],["Able to be trusted or depended on","My old alarm clock is surprisingly reliable for waking me up.","Unreliable, untrustworthy"],["Help or support","I needed emergency assistance tying my tiny shoelaces.","Obstruction, hindrance"],["Able to be checked or proven true","The story about the giant carrot needed to be verifiable before publishing.","Unverifiable, fictional"]]]};
